WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.250
ANDREW HUBERMAN: Welcome
to the Huberman Lab podcast

00:00:02.250 --> 00:00:04.680
where we discuss science
and science-based tools

00:00:04.680 --> 00:00:05.430
for everyday life.

00:00:05.430 --> 00:00:09.130
[MUSIC PLAYING]

00:00:09.130 --> 00:00:10.960
I'm Andrew Huberman,
and I'm a professor

00:00:10.960 --> 00:00:13.090
of neurobiology
and ophthalmology

00:00:13.090 --> 00:00:14.860
at Stanford School of Medicine.

00:00:14.860 --> 00:00:17.290
Today, my guest is
Dr. Kyle Gillett.

00:00:17.290 --> 00:00:20.140
Dr. Kyle Gillett is a dual
board certified physician

00:00:20.140 --> 00:00:23.530
in family medicine and
obesity medicine and an expert

00:00:23.530 --> 00:00:25.150
in hormone optimization.

00:00:25.150 --> 00:00:26.680
He is an M.D--

00:00:26.680 --> 00:00:28.180
that is, a medical doctor--

00:00:28.180 --> 00:00:30.010
and he treats patients
with a variety

00:00:30.010 --> 00:00:32.590
of backgrounds, ages and goals.

00:00:32.590 --> 00:00:35.530
Today, we discuss male
hormone optimization.

00:00:35.530 --> 00:00:39.190
We discuss behavioral tools,
nutrition-based tools,

00:00:39.190 --> 00:00:42.610
supplement-based tools,
prescription-drug-based tools,

00:00:42.610 --> 00:00:46.270
and their interactions in
determining overall levels

00:00:46.270 --> 00:00:48.790
of testosterone,
free testosterone,

00:00:48.790 --> 00:00:52.330
dihydrotestosterone, estrogen,
growth hormone, thyroid

00:00:52.330 --> 00:00:55.330
hormone, and many other
hormones that impact mood,

00:00:55.330 --> 00:00:58.900
libido, well-being,
strength, cognition,

00:00:58.900 --> 00:01:01.300
and various
psychological factors.

00:01:01.300 --> 00:01:02.980
We've covered
hormone optimization

00:01:02.980 --> 00:01:05.170
in both men and women
in previous episodes

00:01:05.170 --> 00:01:07.960
of the Huberman Lab podcast,
but today's discussion

00:01:07.960 --> 00:01:09.160
is different.

00:01:09.160 --> 00:01:12.070
Dr. Kyle Gillett offers very
specific recommendations

00:01:12.070 --> 00:01:15.850
for people with different
goals and of different ages.

00:01:15.850 --> 00:01:18.010
And we get deep
into the weeds of,

00:01:18.010 --> 00:01:20.530
for instance, how does
one know whether or not

00:01:20.530 --> 00:01:24.460
their testosterone is optimized
or not, how often to test

00:01:24.460 --> 00:01:26.410
for specific hormones
such as testosterone

00:01:26.410 --> 00:01:29.350
and other hormones, and
really, how to gauge

00:01:29.350 --> 00:01:31.787
how good one should feel?

00:01:31.787 --> 00:01:34.120
This is something that's often
overlooked in discussions

00:01:34.120 --> 00:01:36.790
about hormone optimization
or health optimization

00:01:36.790 --> 00:01:38.350
of any kind, for that matter.

00:01:38.350 --> 00:01:41.710
For instance, people will
talk about reduced libido

00:01:41.710 --> 00:01:44.350
and discuss whether or not
testosterone levels are

00:01:44.350 --> 00:01:47.038
to blame, but how does
one calibrate their libido

00:01:47.038 --> 00:01:47.830
in the first place?

00:01:47.830 --> 00:01:50.530
That is, how does one know
whether or not their libido is

00:01:50.530 --> 00:01:53.810
normal, too low, or too high?

00:01:53.810 --> 00:01:55.750
We also discuss, for
instance, whether or not

00:01:55.750 --> 00:01:58.292
hormone optimization should
be pursued continually

00:01:58.292 --> 00:01:59.750
throughout the
year-- for instance,

00:01:59.750 --> 00:02:02.080
whether or not you should
cycle on and off supplements

00:02:02.080 --> 00:02:05.630
and/or prescription drugs geared
towards hormone optimization.

00:02:05.630 --> 00:02:08.470
And we discuss the
behavioral foundations

00:02:08.470 --> 00:02:10.180
of optimal hormone function.

00:02:10.180 --> 00:02:12.340
These are things that
every male should be doing

00:02:12.340 --> 00:02:14.320
and various things
they should actively

00:02:14.320 --> 00:02:17.980
avoid if their goal is to
have healthy hormones and to,

00:02:17.980 --> 00:02:21.640
quote, unquote, optimize
their levels of every hormone

00:02:21.640 --> 00:02:23.590
from growth hormone
to testosterone

00:02:23.590 --> 00:02:24.807
at any stage of life.

00:02:24.807 --> 00:02:26.890
And while today's discussion
is about male hormone

00:02:26.890 --> 00:02:28.330
optimization, I
want to emphasize

00:02:28.330 --> 00:02:31.480
that we discuss all the
various ages for male hormone

00:02:31.480 --> 00:02:32.690
optimization.

00:02:32.690 --> 00:02:35.890
So for those of you that are
parents, for those of you that

00:02:35.890 --> 00:02:38.110
are young, those of you that
are middle aged, or old,

00:02:38.110 --> 00:02:43.420
or teenagers, we explore
adolescent, puberty,

00:02:43.420 --> 00:02:46.510
teen and late teens, early
adulthood, adulthood,

00:02:46.510 --> 00:02:48.778
and into the late
geriatric ages.

00:02:48.778 --> 00:02:50.320
So regardless of
your age and whether

00:02:50.320 --> 00:02:52.930
or not you are male or
female, today's episode

00:02:52.930 --> 00:02:54.400
ought to be of interest to you.

00:02:54.400 --> 00:02:56.890
I should also point out
that we will soon also

00:02:56.890 --> 00:03:00.460
be hosting an expert guest on
female hormone optimization.

00:03:00.460 --> 00:03:02.470
One thing that I'm
certain people of all ages

00:03:02.470 --> 00:03:06.040
and biological sex will enjoy
about today's conversation

00:03:06.040 --> 00:03:07.840
is that we also get
into descriptions

00:03:07.840 --> 00:03:11.200
of how psychology and life
events impact hormones

00:03:11.200 --> 00:03:14.080
and how hormones impact
our psychology and the way

00:03:14.080 --> 00:03:16.030
that we show up to
various life events.

00:03:16.030 --> 00:03:18.520
So today is really
a broad overview

00:03:18.520 --> 00:03:22.000
that goes all the way down to
fine details about male hormone

00:03:22.000 --> 00:03:22.690
optimization.

00:03:22.690 --> 00:03:25.040
And I'm certain that by
the end of today's episode,

00:03:25.040 --> 00:03:28.090
you will have an immense amount
of new information about how

00:03:28.090 --> 00:03:30.910
this endocrine-- that is,
hormone system in your body

00:03:30.910 --> 00:03:31.450
works--

00:03:31.450 --> 00:03:35.140
and how it interacts with
your brain and other tissues

00:03:35.140 --> 00:03:39.340
and many, many actionable tools
that you can pursue regardless

00:03:39.340 --> 00:03:40.270
of stage of life.

00:03:40.270 --> 00:03:41.950
Before we begin, I'd
like to emphasize

00:03:41.950 --> 00:03:44.408
that this podcast is separate
from my teaching and research

00:03:44.408 --> 00:03:45.190
roles at Stanford.

00:03:45.190 --> 00:03:47.230
It is, however, part
of my desire and effort

00:03:47.230 --> 00:03:49.240
to bring zero cost to
consumer information

00:03:49.240 --> 00:03:51.400
about science and
science-related tools

00:03:51.400 --> 00:03:52.450
