And then what are some
of the other things

01:16:50.720 --> 01:16:54.657
to optimize testosterone
that are in supplement form?

01:16:54.657 --> 01:16:56.740
KYLE GILLETT: We can talk
about things that affect

01:16:56.740 --> 01:16:58.430
the steroidogenesis cascade.

01:16:58.430 --> 01:16:59.843
So we could touch
on tongkat ali.

01:16:59.843 --> 01:17:02.010
I know we've talked about
that a little bit before--

01:17:02.010 --> 01:17:03.130
ANDREW HUBERMAN: But I'm
guessing a number of people

01:17:03.130 --> 01:17:05.140
probably haven't heard
that conversation.

01:17:05.140 --> 01:17:06.790
KYLE GILLETT: Also
known as Long Jack.

01:17:06.790 --> 01:17:09.940
And that upregulates
several different enzymes

01:17:09.940 --> 01:17:11.920
in the steroidogenesis cascade.

01:17:11.920 --> 01:17:15.650
And by that, what you mean if--
and this is another good thing

01:17:15.650 --> 01:17:16.150
to Google--

01:17:16.150 --> 01:17:18.340
I think anybody interested
in hormone optimization

01:17:18.340 --> 01:17:22.240
should understand where
sterile hormones come from.

01:17:22.240 --> 01:17:24.310
They come usually
from cholesterol

01:17:24.310 --> 01:17:27.320
and they can be shunted off
to vitamin D very easily,

01:17:27.320 --> 01:17:29.590
they can be shunted
off to testosterone,

01:17:29.590 --> 01:17:33.520
or estrogens, or progestins
quite easily as well.

01:17:33.520 --> 01:17:36.190
But tongkat helps
with the conversion

01:17:36.190 --> 01:17:41.680
of multiple key steps where
you synthesize testosterone.

01:17:41.680 --> 01:17:46.060
Another-- think of it as like
a coenzyme or a cofactor--

01:17:46.060 --> 01:17:50.680
an upregulator of these
steps is insulin and IGF-1.

01:17:50.680 --> 01:17:54.790
So a good rule of thumb is if
you are not expecting as much

01:17:54.790 --> 01:17:57.010
growth hormone,
insulin, and IGF-1--

01:17:57.010 --> 01:18:00.790
for example, lower carb
diets, caloric deficits,

01:18:00.790 --> 01:18:03.580
you're trying to cut
body fat or body weight--

01:18:03.580 --> 01:18:07.720
then tongkat is going to
be theoretically especially

01:18:07.720 --> 01:18:08.948
powerful.

01:18:08.948 --> 01:18:10.990
ANDREW HUBERMAN: What
sorts of dosages of tongkat

01:18:10.990 --> 01:18:13.120
do you recommend
to your patients?

01:18:13.120 --> 01:18:17.200
KYLE GILLETT: Anywhere from
300 to 1,200 milligrams a day.

01:18:17.200 --> 01:18:19.990
With tongkat, you need
to be careful with

01:18:19.990 --> 01:18:22.480
the standardization because--

01:18:22.480 --> 01:18:25.030
and if you're thinking about
a general tongkat supplement,

01:18:25.030 --> 01:18:27.520
which is by far the
most well-studied--

01:18:27.520 --> 01:18:32.410
then you're looking at the
eurycomanone content, which

01:18:32.410 --> 01:18:34.870
is a plant compound
that is likely

01:18:34.870 --> 01:18:38.300
the main active
pharmacologic effect.

01:18:38.300 --> 01:18:41.480
So that's the compound that's
having the effect on the body.

01:18:41.480 --> 01:18:45.760
And if you standardize the
eurycomanone very, very high,

01:18:45.760 --> 01:18:49.577
then theoretically you're having
more effect at a lower dose.

01:18:49.577 --> 01:18:51.160
ANDREW HUBERMAN: I
take 400 milligrams

01:18:51.160 --> 01:18:52.828
of tongkat ali per day.

01:18:52.828 --> 01:18:54.370
I take it early in
the day because it

01:18:54.370 --> 01:18:57.310
has a bit of a stimulant effect,
and if I take it after 2:00 PM,

01:18:57.310 --> 01:18:59.560
it starts to inhibit my sleep.

01:18:59.560 --> 01:19:01.690
I've been taking it for years.

01:19:01.690 --> 01:19:05.200
And I rather like
that the effects.

01:19:05.200 --> 01:19:07.510
It seems subtle but consistent.

01:19:07.510 --> 01:19:09.400
I've never cycled it.

01:19:09.400 --> 01:19:11.320
Do you recommend cycling it?

01:19:11.320 --> 01:19:13.390
KYLE GILLETT: I don't see
any reason to cycle it.

01:19:13.390 --> 01:19:17.500
There is a reason to
cycle some supplements,

01:19:17.500 --> 01:19:19.205
but no reason to cycle tongkat.

01:19:19.205 --> 01:19:20.830
ANDREW HUBERMAN: My
blood work tells me

01:19:20.830 --> 01:19:23.890
that it causes an increase
in free testosterone for me

01:19:23.890 --> 01:19:27.940
and also a slight increase in
luteinizing hormone for me.

01:19:27.940 --> 01:19:30.340
What are some of the other
effects on various hormones

01:19:30.340 --> 01:19:32.770
that you've observed in the
bloodwork of your patients

01:19:32.770 --> 01:19:34.920
taking tongkat ali?

01:19:34.920 --> 01:19:38.190
KYLE GILLETT: Tongkat can
also slightly increase DHEA.

01:19:38.190 --> 01:19:41.220
And if you have a
very high SHBG--

01:19:41.220 --> 01:19:43.920
again, that's the protein
that binds up your androgens

01:19:43.920 --> 01:19:47.550
and estrogens-- an extremely
important protein--

01:19:47.550 --> 01:19:51.250
the higher your SHBG, the
more it helps decrease it.

01:19:51.250 --> 01:19:54.720
So they've studied
tongkat in populations

01:19:54.720 --> 01:19:58.402
with very normal SHBGs and
it does nothing for SHBG.

01:19:58.402 --> 01:19:59.610
ANDREW HUBERMAN: Interesting.

01:19:59.610 --> 01:20:02.260
Does that mean it does
nothing for somebody overall?

01:20:02.260 --> 01:20:05.100
So if somebody has an SHBG
that's in the normal range,

01:20:05.100 --> 01:20:08.160
will taking tongkat benefit
them in any other way?

01:20:08.160 --> 01:20:11.070
KYLE GILLETT: Yes, it'll
increase their total and free

01:20:11.070 --> 01:20:12.120
testosterone.

01:20:12.120 --> 01:20:13.948
ANDREW HUBERMAN: Got it.

01:20:13.948 --> 01:20:15.990
Does it-- is it known to
have effects on anything

01:20:15.990 --> 01:20:18.030
else like thyroid
hormone, growth hormone,

01:20:18.030 --> 01:20:21.120
or is it purely in these
steroid synthesis pathways?

01:20:21.120 --> 01:20:24.240
Or steroid-- I should say
synthesis, and receptor,

01:20:24.240 --> 01:20:25.680
and modulation pathways.

01:20:25.680 --> 01:20:28.260
KYLE GILLETT: There's no direct
effect on those pathways.

01:20:28.260 --> 01:20:34.560
However, any time you alter your
free androgen or free estrogen,

01:20:34.560 --> 01:20:37.630
particularly one without
altering the other,

01:20:37.630 --> 01:20:39.270
it will alter the
binding protein

01:20:39.270 --> 01:20:41.050
that binds thyroid hormones.

01:20:41.050 --> 01:20:43.170
So any change you
make, whether it's

01:20:43.170 --> 01:20:45.810
natural optimization
or hormone replacement,

01:20:45.810 --> 01:20:49.170
you're going to slightly skew
your thyroid hormone profile.

01:20:49.170 --> 01:20:52.620
One common actionable example
of this that I see often

01:20:52.620 --> 01:20:56.670
clinically is someone
starts, let's say,

01:20:56.670 --> 01:20:59.340
estrogen replacement or
testosterone replacement--

01:20:59.340 --> 01:21:01.560
maybe they're taking an
AI with their testosterone

01:21:01.560 --> 01:21:02.280
replacement--

01:21:02.280 --> 01:21:03.822
ANDREW HUBERMAN:
Aromatase inhibitor?

01:21:03.822 --> 01:21:05.738
KYLE GILLETT: Correct,
an aromatase inhibitor,

01:21:05.738 --> 01:21:07.740
which blocks the
conversion to estrogen.

01:21:07.740 --> 01:21:10.680
If they're taking
testosterone and they have

01:21:10.680 --> 01:21:12.870
very little
estrogen, then you're

01:21:12.870 --> 01:21:15.780
going to decrease the
binding protein, also known

01:21:15.780 --> 01:21:19.530
as thyroxine binding globulin,
which binds active thyroid

01:21:19.530 --> 01:21:20.560
hormones.

01:21:20.560 --> 01:21:24.690
So if you start
TRT and you either

01:21:24.690 --> 01:21:28.530
have low aromatase activity
or no aromatase activity--

01:21:28.530 --> 01:21:31.800
no conversion to estrogen--
then your free thyroid hormones

01:21:31.800 --> 01:21:33.300
will go up.

01:21:33.300 --> 01:21:36.820
Even just acutely, usually
feedback inhibition,

01:21:36.820 --> 01:21:39.870
which is how the body
talks to itself and says,

01:21:39.870 --> 01:21:42.300
we need to make more of
this or less of this.

01:21:42.300 --> 01:21:46.080
But acutely, there's
not always enough time.

01:21:46.080 --> 01:21:49.260
You're going to have very
high thyroid hormones

01:21:49.260 --> 01:21:52.650
and you can have tachycardia,
which is a fast heart rate

01:21:52.650 --> 01:21:54.720
or you can feel kind
of like overly fight

01:21:54.720 --> 01:21:57.390
or flight due to
increased thyroid hormone

01:21:57.390 --> 01:21:59.520
activity in the in tissue.

01:21:59.520 --> 01:22:00.870
ANDREW HUBERMAN: Interesting.

01:22:00.870 --> 01:22:03.120
So tongkat ali--
just a broad range--

01:22:03.120 --> 01:22:05.160
300 to 1,200 milligrams per day.

01:22:05.160 --> 01:22:08.160
And I realize that the
source matters there.

01:22:08.160 --> 01:22:10.320
What are some of
the other hormones

01:22:10.320 --> 01:22:13.800
that you prescribe to
your patients who do not

01:22:13.800 --> 01:22:16.140
want to go on testosterone
replacement therapy

01:22:16.140 --> 01:22:20.280
or take exogenous DHEA
or anything like that?

01:22:20.280 --> 01:22:22.410
KYLE GILLETT: We can
talk about fadogia next.

01:22:22.410 --> 01:22:25.110
Fadogia is interesting because--
it's a genus of plants.

01:22:25.110 --> 01:22:27.060
Fadogia agrestis is one of them.

01:22:27.060 --> 01:22:30.180
There's many others that
are very interesting.

01:22:30.180 --> 01:22:32.820
That species is likely
the most well-studied,

01:22:32.820 --> 01:22:37.020
and it will increase
LH, so I would not

01:22:37.020 --> 01:22:39.900
consider it an LH mimetic,
so it doesn't really mimetic.

01:22:39.900 --> 01:22:42.390
But it increases the release
of luteinizing hormone

01:22:42.390 --> 01:22:43.290
from the pituitary.

01:22:43.290 --> 01:22:46.500
That's a hormone that
binds to the Leydig cell

01:22:46.500 --> 01:22:49.560
to the LH receptor
kind of like hCG does.

01:22:49.560 --> 01:22:52.712
And it will increase the
release of testosterone.

01:22:52.712 --> 01:22:53.670
ANDREW HUBERMAN: I see.

01:22:53.670 --> 01:22:56.460
So I think for people who
aren't familiar with hCG--

01:22:56.460 --> 01:22:58.200
so human chorionic
gonadotropin--

01:22:58.200 --> 01:23:00.247
is basically synthetic
luteinizing hormone

01:23:00.247 --> 01:23:01.830
and luteinizing
hormone is the hormone

01:23:01.830 --> 01:23:03.288
released from the
pituitary that is

01:23:03.288 --> 01:23:05.130
going to travel
down to the testes

01:23:05.130 --> 01:23:08.550
to stimulate the production
of sperm and testosterone,

01:23:08.550 --> 01:23:09.780
but mainly testosterone.

01:23:09.780 --> 01:23:11.670
Is that correct?

01:23:11.670 --> 01:23:13.350
KYLE GILLETT: Mostly correct.

01:23:13.350 --> 01:23:15.360
Technically,
synthetic LH is also

01:23:15.360 --> 01:23:18.330
known as little r LH,
or recombinant LH.

01:23:18.330 --> 01:23:22.320
And hCG can be
synthetic, but often, it

01:23:22.320 --> 01:23:24.510
is just refined from the
urine of pregnant ladies

01:23:24.510 --> 01:23:27.790
since the placenta makes it.

01:23:27.790 --> 01:23:30.443
That's why it's called
chorionic gonadotropin.

01:23:30.443 --> 01:23:31.860
ANDREW HUBERMAN:
So where are they

01:23:31.860 --> 01:23:35.070
getting all this
pregnant women's urine?

01:23:35.070 --> 01:23:37.785
I mean, there a location?

01:23:37.785 --> 01:23:39.660
I mean, not that I want
to go there, I just--

01:23:39.660 --> 01:23:40.200
KYLE GILLETT: Donation?

01:23:40.200 --> 01:23:41.160
ANDREW HUBERMAN: --really--
so there are women that--

01:23:41.160 --> 01:23:42.900
KYLE GILLETT: First
trimester pregnant ladies.

01:23:42.900 --> 01:23:43.530
It's very high.

01:23:43.530 --> 01:23:45.113
ANDREW HUBERMAN:
Donating their urine,

01:23:45.113 --> 01:23:48.990
and then they're purifying it,
and then men are injecting it?

01:23:48.990 --> 01:23:49.830
KYLE GILLETT: Yes.

01:23:49.830 --> 01:23:50.550
ANDREW HUBERMAN: Wow.

01:23:50.550 --> 01:23:51.510
KYLE GILLETT: And
that's actually

01:23:51.510 --> 01:23:53.190
the same for menopausal ladies.

01:23:53.190 --> 01:23:55.140
So first trimester
pregnant ladies,

01:23:55.140 --> 01:24:00.420
that's how you can
make non-synthetic hCG.

01:24:00.420 --> 01:24:04.140
And then for menotropins
which are also known--

01:24:04.140 --> 01:24:07.470
there's a couple of different
names for it, like menopur.

01:24:07.470 --> 01:24:10.710
You have menopausal ladies
that have very high LH and FSH,

01:24:10.710 --> 01:24:13.770
and then you refine
the FSH and LH.

01:24:13.770 --> 01:24:17.280
ANDREW HUBERMAN: So moving
away from the sources

01:24:17.280 --> 01:24:21.510
and from urine, Fadogia
agrestis, what dosages

01:24:21.510 --> 01:24:23.100
do you have patients take?

01:24:23.100 --> 01:24:26.040
I've heard of some
potential toxicity

01:24:26.040 --> 01:24:27.510
to the testicular cells.

01:24:27.510 --> 01:24:28.930
KYLE GILLETT: There
is one study--

01:24:28.930 --> 01:24:33.060
and this is a rat study, but you
can equate the dose of toxicity

01:24:33.060 --> 01:24:34.080
in rats and humans.

01:24:34.080 --> 01:24:36.880
They did not give these
rats any antioxidants,

01:24:36.880 --> 01:24:41.450
but it increases a couple
of different proinflammatory

01:24:41.450 --> 01:24:41.950
markers.

01:24:41.950 --> 01:24:44.670
One is GGT, or gamma
glutamate transferase.

01:24:44.670 --> 01:24:46.900
It comes from both the
testes and the liver,

01:24:46.900 --> 01:24:51.010
and one is alkaline phosphatase,
also known as Alkphos, again,

01:24:51.010 --> 01:24:52.392
coming from both areas.

01:24:52.392 --> 01:24:54.100
There are several
different ways that you

01:24:54.100 --> 01:24:55.700
can attenuate this increase.

01:24:55.700 --> 01:24:58.480
And you can also just check
to see if you have increased.

01:24:58.480 --> 01:25:02.110
In the rat dose that equates
with humans that had no

01:25:02.110 --> 01:25:03.850
effect-- so the safe dose--

01:25:03.850 --> 01:25:06.490
was an average of
300 milligrams a day.

01:25:06.490 --> 01:25:08.740
ANDREW HUBERMAN: So that
would be 300 milligrams a day

01:25:08.740 --> 01:25:12.710
in humans is the dosage
that did not have toxicity.

01:25:12.710 --> 01:25:13.210
Correct?

01:25:13.210 --> 01:25:14.127
KYLE GILLETT: Correct.

01:25:14.127 --> 01:25:17.770
And often, even if there
is toxicity in rats,

01:25:17.770 --> 01:25:19.460
there is not toxicity in humans.

01:25:19.460 --> 01:25:23.440
So it's not directly
equitable, but to be safe,

01:25:23.440 --> 01:25:26.620
another regimen that I have
people take is 600 milligrams

01:25:26.620 --> 01:25:28.900
every other day
or 600 milligrams

01:25:28.900 --> 01:25:31.948
three times a week-- often
Monday, Wednesday, Friday.

01:25:31.948 --> 01:25:34.240
ANDREW HUBERMAN: This is very
interesting and relevant,

01:25:34.240 --> 01:25:37.450
because I've been taking
fadogia for some period of time.

01:25:37.450 --> 01:25:40.390
All my markers
and tests indicate

01:25:40.390 --> 01:25:41.770
that there's no toxicity.

01:25:41.770 --> 01:25:45.350
But I've been taking
600 milligrams per day,

01:25:45.350 --> 01:25:49.480
but I've been cycling it for
about 8 to 12 weeks on and then

01:25:49.480 --> 01:25:50.560
a few weeks off.

01:25:50.560 --> 01:25:52.150
But based on what
you're saying, I'm

01:25:52.150 --> 01:25:54.873
thinking maybe three times
per week or every other day

01:25:54.873 --> 01:25:55.540
might be better.

01:25:55.540 --> 01:25:56.355
Is that right?

01:25:56.355 --> 01:25:58.480
KYLE GILLETT: If you weren't
going to get any labs,

01:25:58.480 --> 01:26:00.430
that is certainly the
regimen that you want.

01:26:00.430 --> 01:26:03.430
If you're going to check
your GGT and ALK phos,

01:26:03.430 --> 01:26:06.730
or even take other things to
prevent those from increasing,

01:26:06.730 --> 01:26:10.990
then you can certainly be more
aggressive with your fadogia

01:26:10.990 --> 01:26:11.860
dosing.

01:26:11.860 --> 01:26:13.870
You can increase it
quite a bit, and it

01:26:13.870 --> 01:26:18.070
has a dose dependent response in
both the activities associated

01:26:18.070 --> 01:26:22.210
with high testosterone and
also just LH and testosterone.

01:26:22.210 --> 01:26:24.220
So the more aggressive
regimen would

01:26:24.220 --> 01:26:26.950
be 600 milligrams
daily for a month

01:26:26.950 --> 01:26:28.542
and then take one
to two weeks off.

01:26:28.542 --> 01:26:29.500
ANDREW HUBERMAN: Great.

01:26:29.500 --> 01:26:32.890
I think that's more or
less what I've been doing.

01:26:32.890 --> 01:26:33.850
Terrific.

01:26:33.850 --> 01:26:35.770
In terms of other
hormones, what are

01:26:35.770 --> 01:26:38.675
some of the supplements that
can support growth hormone--

01:26:38.675 --> 01:26:40.300
a hormone that's
associated with tissue

01:26:40.300 --> 01:26:43.900
repair and, in some cases,
metabolism and fat loss?

01:26:43.900 --> 01:26:46.750
What are some of the
tools, nutritional and/or

01:26:46.750 --> 01:26:51.830
supplement-based, one can do
to tap on the growth hormone

01:26:51.830 --> 01:26:52.330
pathway?

01:26:52.330 --> 01:26:54.400
And let's lump
IGF-1 in there too

01:26:54.400 --> 01:26:55.870
since they're
essentially working

01:26:55.870 --> 01:26:57.452
along the same dimensions.

01:26:57.452 --> 01:26:59.410
KYLE GILLETT: A quick
synopsis-- growth hormone

01:26:59.410 --> 01:27:04.210
is a peptide hormone, and it
is released by the pituitary.

01:27:04.210 --> 01:27:07.315
There's growth hormone
releasing hormone and ghrelin

01:27:07.315 --> 01:27:08.440
that stimulate the release.

01:27:08.440 --> 01:27:11.950
So there's also peptides that
are very analogous to these two

01:27:11.950 --> 01:27:13.240
things.

01:27:13.240 --> 01:27:15.610
You have that
pulsatile secretion

01:27:15.610 --> 01:27:18.460
of growth hormone in a very
fast half life of just minutes,

01:27:18.460 --> 01:27:20.650
and then it increases IGF-1.

01:27:20.650 --> 01:27:24.490
There is both peripheral IGF-1
and central IGF-1 and IGF2,

01:27:24.490 --> 01:27:27.580
but no need to get
into the specifics.

01:27:27.580 --> 01:27:31.090
There is a happy medium to
where your growth hormone is

01:27:31.090 --> 01:27:34.540
at an adequate level and your
IGF-1 is an adequate level.

01:27:34.540 --> 01:27:36.620
Usually, those
two are congruent.

01:27:36.620 --> 01:27:40.540
So in most cases, we just check
an IGF-1 and, occasionally,

01:27:40.540 --> 01:27:42.730
the binding peptides
for IGF-1 kind

01:27:42.730 --> 01:27:45.100
of like SHBG that we
talked about earlier,

01:27:45.100 --> 01:27:49.000
but you're estimating
a free IGF-1.

01:27:49.000 --> 01:27:51.550
It's kind of confusing
because all hormone--

01:27:51.550 --> 01:27:55.270
almost all hormones have binding
proteins to help regulate them.

01:27:55.270 --> 01:27:57.670
But often, you want to
look at free testosterone,

01:27:57.670 --> 01:28:00.280
free estradiol, free IGF-1--

01:28:00.280 --> 01:28:03.040
or at least estimate
it-- free cortisol even,

01:28:03.040 --> 01:28:05.680
and free thyroid hormone.

01:28:05.680 --> 01:28:10.630
But when you're talking about
growth hormone and IGF-1,

01:28:10.630 --> 01:28:14.140
usually you don't need to
do anything to optimize it.

01:28:14.140 --> 01:28:18.370
If you are diabetic,
then-- and depending

01:28:18.370 --> 01:28:21.700
on the type of diabetes,
your IGF-1 and growth hormone

01:28:21.700 --> 01:28:23.530
can be too high.

01:28:23.530 --> 01:28:25.910
Specifically, in
type 1 diabetes,

01:28:25.910 --> 01:28:29.830
your growth hormone is extremely
high, but your IGF-1 is low.

01:28:29.830 --> 01:28:33.040
So if you're in a dysregulated
state or have pathology,

01:28:33.040 --> 01:28:37.330
I would just talk to your doctor
about IGF-1 or growth hormone.

01:28:37.330 --> 01:28:39.400
Taking amino acids
before you go to bed

01:28:39.400 --> 01:28:42.070
could potentially help
with growth hormone release

01:28:42.070 --> 01:28:46.553
just because most growth hormone
is released while you sleep.

01:28:46.553 --> 01:28:48.220
ANDREW HUBERMAN: I've
heard that fasting

01:28:48.220 --> 01:28:49.850
can increase growth hormone.

01:28:49.850 --> 01:28:52.960
And I know there are certain
patterns of weight training

01:28:52.960 --> 01:28:54.640
that can increase
growth hormone.

01:28:54.640 --> 01:28:57.040
Some of those regimens
in the weight room

01:28:57.040 --> 01:29:01.240
that increase growth hormone
have been covered by Dr. Duncan

01:29:01.240 --> 01:29:04.480
French, who was a
guest on this podcast,

01:29:04.480 --> 01:29:08.860
and so maybe we'll refer
people to that episode

01:29:08.860 --> 01:29:11.983
for the specific protocols--
these high volume training.

01:29:11.983 --> 01:29:13.900
KYLE GILLETT: During
those training exercises,

01:29:13.900 --> 01:29:17.600
it usually does it transiently
for a period of a few hours.

01:29:17.600 --> 01:29:22.820
And a lot of this IGF-1 is
released by the muscle itself.

01:29:22.820 --> 01:29:25.330
So it's not necessarily
released by the liver.

01:29:25.330 --> 01:29:28.840
IGF-1 that is released
directly due to growth hormone

01:29:28.840 --> 01:29:31.120
signaling-- usually, the
growth hormone comes from

01:29:31.120 --> 01:29:34.120
the pituitary and binds to
the liver where usually,

01:29:34.120 --> 01:29:35.800
it has a half life
of about a week,

01:29:35.800 --> 01:29:37.720
where the paracrine
or autocrine--

01:29:37.720 --> 01:29:40.510
think of it as like the
peripherally acting or acting

01:29:40.510 --> 01:29:43.630
in the muscles itself,
which is also helpful--

01:29:43.630 --> 01:29:47.680
is released and is not as
concerning because it's not

01:29:47.680 --> 01:29:51.190
related to insulin
resistance, but it is

01:29:51.190 --> 01:29:53.440
related to the training itself.

01:29:53.440 --> 01:29:57.120
ANDREW HUBERMAN: So fasting
and growth hormone--

01:29:57.120 --> 01:29:59.700
is it true that fasting can
increase growth hormone?

01:29:59.700 --> 01:30:03.510
And maybe as a little
related tangent,

01:30:03.510 --> 01:30:06.383
I've heard that limiting
food intake for the two hours

01:30:06.383 --> 01:30:07.800
before going to
sleep can increase

01:30:07.800 --> 01:30:10.650
the pulse of growth hormone that
one experiences during sleep.

01:30:10.650 --> 01:30:13.317
Of course, everyone gets a pulse
of growth hormone during sleep,

01:30:13.317 --> 01:30:15.510
but especially
carbohydrate-laden meals

01:30:15.510 --> 01:30:19.110
can blunt that peak that
occurs during sleep quite

01:30:19.110 --> 01:30:19.900
substantially.

01:30:19.900 --> 01:30:25.320
So two questions-- does avoiding
food intake in the two hours

01:30:25.320 --> 01:30:28.020
prior to sleep help increase
growth hormone release?

01:30:28.020 --> 01:30:29.550
Maybe it's being
overly neurotic.

01:30:29.550 --> 01:30:33.270
Maybe people need to avoid food
in the four hours before sleep.

01:30:33.270 --> 01:30:36.405
But regardless, what is the
relationship between fasting

01:30:36.405 --> 01:30:37.530
and growth hormone release?

01:30:37.530 --> 01:30:38.880
I find this really interesting.

01:30:38.880 --> 01:30:41.700
KYLE GILLETT: Fasting
certainly potently increases

01:30:41.700 --> 01:30:43.240
growth hormone release.

01:30:43.240 --> 01:30:49.510
However, the IND binding to
the receptor is less sensitive.

01:30:49.510 --> 01:30:53.370
So although fasting does
increase growth hormone,

01:30:53.370 --> 01:30:55.830
the genes that are
downstream to it--

01:30:55.830 --> 01:30:58.710
both the growth
hormone genes and IGF-1

01:30:58.710 --> 01:31:02.730
related gene transcription
activity-- will not

01:31:02.730 --> 01:31:04.600
be significantly higher.

01:31:04.600 --> 01:31:08.880
However, if you are optimizing
the growth hormone that

01:31:08.880 --> 01:31:12.450
is released as a
pulsatile secretion,

01:31:12.450 --> 01:31:15.030
it is helpful to avoid
eating for two hours.

01:31:15.030 --> 01:31:17.550
So the general rule of thumb
is avoid eating about two hours

01:31:17.550 --> 01:31:18.090
before bed.

01:31:18.090 --> 01:31:20.460
I think that's clinically
significant and helpful.

01:31:20.460 --> 01:31:23.550
But fasting otherwise
specifically for growth hormone

01:31:23.550 --> 01:31:25.860
optimization in
someone who already

01:31:25.860 --> 01:31:29.280
has normal growth hormone
signaling is not helpful.

01:31:29.280 --> 01:31:31.680
ANDREW HUBERMAN:
That's extremely useful

01:31:31.680 --> 01:31:33.778
to hear because one
of the major reasons

01:31:33.778 --> 01:31:36.070
why people fast is to get
that growth hormone increase.

01:31:36.070 --> 01:31:39.450
But if they're adjusting things
on the backend that negate

01:31:39.450 --> 01:31:42.872
that, well, then, no such luck.

01:31:42.872 --> 01:31:44.580
Not that I have anything
against fasting.

01:31:44.580 --> 01:31:46.770
I do a pseudointermittent
fasting mostly

01:31:46.770 --> 01:31:51.127
because I prefer to eat at
fairly regular times of day.

01:31:51.127 --> 01:31:52.710
So it doesn't sound
like there's a lot

01:31:52.710 --> 01:31:54.720
that people can take
in supplement form

01:31:54.720 --> 01:31:55.830
to improve growth hormone.

01:31:55.830 --> 01:31:56.880
What about thyroid hormone?

01:31:56.880 --> 01:31:59.505
What are some of the things that
people can take or do in order

01:31:59.505 --> 01:32:04.397
to make sure that their thyroid
hormone levels are appropriate?

01:32:04.397 --> 01:32:06.480
KYLE GILLETT: You want to
have a balance of iodine

01:32:06.480 --> 01:32:08.355
and you want to have a
good source of iodine.

01:32:08.355 --> 01:32:10.020
So there are some
camps that say you

01:32:10.020 --> 01:32:12.750
should use a huge
high dose of iodine

01:32:12.750 --> 01:32:14.138
and there's protocols for it.

01:32:14.138 --> 01:32:16.680
And there are some that say you
should use just barely enough

01:32:16.680 --> 01:32:17.580
iodine--

01:32:17.580 --> 01:32:20.410
I believe it's like
200 micrograms per day.

01:32:20.410 --> 01:32:22.570
But you want to balance.

01:32:22.570 --> 01:32:25.380
One of the things that I
see that many people do not

01:32:25.380 --> 01:32:28.620
talk about when it comes
to iodine and thyroid

01:32:28.620 --> 01:32:33.060
is there's compounds
known as goitrogens.

01:32:33.060 --> 01:32:36.210
And these goitrogens are
neither good nor evil,

01:32:36.210 --> 01:32:39.420
but they're actually kind
of a nice check and balance.

01:32:39.420 --> 01:32:42.630
You need more iodine if you
consume more goitrogens.

01:32:42.630 --> 01:32:46.470
And some examples of these are
some of my favorite foods--

01:32:46.470 --> 01:32:48.000
cruciferous vegetables.

01:32:48.000 --> 01:32:52.650
Boron is also a goitrogen.
So higher goitrogens,

01:32:52.650 --> 01:32:54.510
higher iodine.

01:32:54.510 --> 01:32:56.670
ANDREW HUBERMAN:
So ingesting iodine

01:32:56.670 --> 01:32:58.410
containing salt is useful?

01:32:58.410 --> 01:33:00.100
Yes or no?

01:33:00.100 --> 01:33:02.770
KYLE GILLETT: Iodized
salt does prevent goiter,

01:33:02.770 --> 01:33:06.970
but it is not necessarily
the ideal form of iodine.

01:33:06.970 --> 01:33:09.640
Good forms of iodine
often come from the ocean.

01:33:09.640 --> 01:33:12.310
If you look at a chart
of hypothyroidism,

01:33:12.310 --> 01:33:15.310
there is a tendency to have
more hypothyroidism the more

01:33:15.310 --> 01:33:17.160
inland you go.

01:33:17.160 --> 01:33:20.460
ANDREW HUBERMAN: So trying to
eat some cruciferous vegetables

01:33:20.460 --> 01:33:24.240
each day would be the best way
to improve thyroid hormone.

01:33:24.240 --> 01:33:26.010
KYLE GILLETT: Along
with plenty of iodine.

01:33:26.010 --> 01:33:28.020
You don't want too
much iodine signaling.

01:33:28.020 --> 01:33:31.170
Many people are familiar with
radioactive iodine tablets,

01:33:31.170 --> 01:33:34.020
and that's basically an
extremely high amount of iodine

01:33:34.020 --> 01:33:38.370
to block out the
radioactive iodine that

01:33:38.370 --> 01:33:42.040
comes from after like a
nuclear meltdown or whatnot.

01:33:42.040 --> 01:33:47.020
ANDREW HUBERMAN: So we've got
creatine, betaine, l-carnitine,

01:33:47.020 --> 01:33:50.620
with allicin garlic
to offset the TMAO.

01:33:50.620 --> 01:33:55.740
Vitamin D3, boron, tongkat
ali, fadogia, some fasting.

01:33:55.740 --> 01:33:58.060
I'd love to talk to
you about peptides.

01:33:58.060 --> 01:33:59.920
So I can imagine a hierarchy.

01:33:59.920 --> 01:34:03.323
A hierarchy starts with
behaviors and nutrition.

01:34:03.323 --> 01:34:04.990
Behaviors, of course,
includes training,

01:34:04.990 --> 01:34:08.200
and limiting stress, and all the
things we talked about before--

01:34:08.200 --> 01:34:12.280
sunshine et cetera--
and optimize nutrition.

01:34:12.280 --> 01:34:15.190
Then, we talked
about supplements--

01:34:15.190 --> 01:34:19.060
all the things we just listed
off to optimize testosterone.

01:34:19.060 --> 01:34:21.158
And we can get into
this, but estrogen

01:34:21.158 --> 01:34:23.200
as well, which is important
for libido, and brain

01:34:23.200 --> 01:34:25.760
function, and tissue function,
and joints feeling good, et

01:34:25.760 --> 01:34:26.410
cetera.

01:34:26.410 --> 01:34:29.470
But then we get into the realm
where one might, or could

01:34:29.470 --> 01:34:31.450
consider, exogenous hormones.

01:34:31.450 --> 01:34:33.280
Get-- taking a small
dose of testosterone

01:34:33.280 --> 01:34:37.932
or taking a small dose of GH
even if that were appropriate

01:34:37.932 --> 01:34:39.640
and certainly only
working with a doctor.

01:34:39.640 --> 01:34:42.785
But in between, there's a
step of so-called peptides.

01:34:42.785 --> 01:34:44.410
And of course, there
are many peptides.

01:34:44.410 --> 01:34:45.860
We've already talked
about some of them.

01:34:45.860 --> 01:34:47.652
But when people talk
about taking peptides,

01:34:47.652 --> 01:34:49.300
the ones that I hear
most often about

01:34:49.300 --> 01:34:55.420
is a category that
increases GH and IGF-1,

01:34:55.420 --> 01:35:03.190
and those to my knowledge go by
the things like sermorelin sort

01:35:03.190 --> 01:35:06.250
of a kit of things that
are taken separately

01:35:06.250 --> 01:35:09.430
or in combination to
increase GH and IGF-1.

01:35:09.430 --> 01:35:11.080
But then other
people, for instance,

01:35:11.080 --> 01:35:15.670
are taking peptides like
BPC 157 to try and improve

01:35:15.670 --> 01:35:17.380
tissue healing and recovery.

01:35:17.380 --> 01:35:19.870
There's a lot of
interest in peptides.

01:35:19.870 --> 01:35:22.450
Please, if you would,
tell us about what

01:35:22.450 --> 01:35:24.190
you know about the
safety of peptides

01:35:24.190 --> 01:35:27.490
in terms of their sourcing
and the utility of peptides.

01:35:27.490 --> 01:35:30.430
Is this something that people
should consider before thinking

01:35:30.430 --> 01:35:31.600
about hormone replacement?

01:35:31.600 --> 01:35:33.520
Should people be
wary of these things?

01:35:33.520 --> 01:35:35.860
I am very wary of
particular sources that are

01:35:35.860 --> 01:35:37.990
sold online that are not clean.

01:35:37.990 --> 01:35:40.240
They contain contaminants
and that could be dangerous.

01:35:40.240 --> 01:35:42.280
I really would love your
thoughts on peptides.

01:35:42.280 --> 01:35:45.330
So I'm just going to sit back
and let you riff on peptides,

01:35:45.330 --> 01:35:47.830
but if you could touch on some
of the ones that I mentioned,

01:35:47.830 --> 01:35:50.020
I'd be most grateful.

01:35:50.020 --> 01:35:52.120
KYLE GILLETT: A
peptide is just a chain

01:35:52.120 --> 01:35:55.960
of amino acids between two and
a couple hundred in length.

01:35:55.960 --> 01:35:59.410
So I think of peptides as
several different categories.

01:35:59.410 --> 01:36:02.050
And the GHRPs that
you mentioned,

01:36:02.050 --> 01:36:03.430
I would consider those--

01:36:03.430 --> 01:36:06.790
and that stands for Growth
Hormone Releasing Peptide.

01:36:06.790 --> 01:36:08.840
You have two main types--

01:36:08.840 --> 01:36:13.450
the ghrelin agonist that
are-- or they hit the ghrelin

01:36:13.450 --> 01:36:17.960
receptor, and it helps release
growth hormone because of that.

01:36:17.960 --> 01:36:21.970
And then also the
GHRH-like peptides.

01:36:21.970 --> 01:36:24.130
So they're very similar to
growth hormone releasing

01:36:24.130 --> 01:36:24.640
hormone.

01:36:24.640 --> 01:36:27.280
Often, they just change
a couple amino acids,

01:36:27.280 --> 01:36:29.410
and it acts like that.

01:36:29.410 --> 01:36:32.860
Tesamorelin is one of them,
sermorelin is another one,

01:36:32.860 --> 01:36:36.160
and CJC is another common one.

01:36:36.160 --> 01:36:40.210
I believe those are all in the
class of GHRH-like peptides,

01:36:40.210 --> 01:36:43.540
whereas ipamorelin or
ibutamoren, which is also

01:36:43.540 --> 01:36:48.230
known as MK-677, those two
are in the class of ghrelin

01:36:48.230 --> 01:36:48.730
agonist.

01:36:48.730 --> 01:36:50.830
So they're more like
they hit the receptor

01:36:50.830 --> 01:36:54.070
that ghrelin does whereas
the other ones hit the GHRH

01:36:54.070 --> 01:36:54.760
receptor.

01:36:54.760 --> 01:36:56.860
ANDREW HUBERMAN: I think of
ghrelin as making me hungry.

01:36:56.860 --> 01:36:57.910
KYLE GILLETT: Hungry and angry.

01:36:57.910 --> 01:36:59.285
ANDREW HUBERMAN:
Why would I want

01:36:59.285 --> 01:37:02.260
to take something that would
increase ghrelin signaling?

01:37:02.260 --> 01:37:04.670
KYLE GILLETT: Some people
are trying to gain weight.

01:37:04.670 --> 01:37:06.770
It also does increase
your growth hormone.

01:37:06.770 --> 01:37:09.760
So if your growth hormone is
very low, you can consider it.

01:37:09.760 --> 01:37:13.720
Ibutamoren is a long-acting--
so it has a long half life, also

01:37:13.720 --> 01:37:14.470
known as MK-677.

01:37:14.470 --> 01:37:17.560
It was well-- it
was studied mostly

01:37:17.560 --> 01:37:19.780
in growth hormone deficiency.

01:37:19.780 --> 01:37:22.332
ANDREW HUBERMAN: And do
these people get angry also?

01:37:22.332 --> 01:37:23.290
KYLE GILLETT: They can.

01:37:23.290 --> 01:37:27.340
Many people report a
side effect of anxiety

01:37:27.340 --> 01:37:29.200
or significant hunger.

01:37:29.200 --> 01:37:31.090
Most people take
it in the evening

01:37:31.090 --> 01:37:33.740
so they don't notice
that hunger as much.

01:37:33.740 --> 01:37:36.232
It can also greatly
increase your blood glucose.

01:37:36.232 --> 01:37:38.190
So if you're insulin
resistant or pre-diabetic,

01:37:38.190 --> 01:37:40.765
it gets especially concerning.

01:37:40.765 --> 01:37:43.390
ANDREW HUBERMAN: This is one of
those rare moments where I hear

01:37:43.390 --> 01:37:48.250
something and I think, even
though there is this kit

01:37:48.250 --> 01:37:50.530
of compounds that can
increase GH and IGF-1,

01:37:50.530 --> 01:37:52.570
based on everything
you're telling me,

01:37:52.570 --> 01:37:56.050
maybe just taking GH is the
better option for those people,

01:37:56.050 --> 01:37:58.060
because growth hormone,
at least it's--

01:37:58.060 --> 01:37:59.770
synthetic growth
hormone is mimicking

01:37:59.770 --> 01:38:01.090
an endogenous hormone.

01:38:01.090 --> 01:38:04.557
I mean, certainly not taking
anything might be the ideal.

01:38:04.557 --> 01:38:06.640
But for those that want
to increase growth hormone

01:38:06.640 --> 01:38:08.015
and they want to
use pharmacology

01:38:08.015 --> 01:38:12.547
to do that, it sounds like these
peptides are pretty precarious.

01:38:12.547 --> 01:38:14.880
KYLE GILLETT: Yeah, it kind
of depends on the situation.

01:38:14.880 --> 01:38:19.370
If there's an individual
that struggles with hunger

01:38:19.370 --> 01:38:20.450
and not eating enough--

01:38:20.450 --> 01:38:25.700
for example, someone who has
a very small stomach or they

01:38:25.700 --> 01:38:27.950
just have a very
low hunger drive,

01:38:27.950 --> 01:38:31.940
sometimes you want more of
that orexigenic signaling.

01:38:31.940 --> 01:38:34.880
The hypothalamus, you have
anorexia signaling, which

01:38:34.880 --> 01:38:37.830
is kind of like anorexia,
and orexigenic signaling,

01:38:37.830 --> 01:38:38.600
which is--

01:38:38.600 --> 01:38:42.410
I call it the hangry
center of the hypothalamus

01:38:42.410 --> 01:38:43.880
or the hangry center.

01:38:43.880 --> 01:38:47.150
And if there's an imbalance
between those two, then

01:38:47.150 --> 01:38:49.040
perhaps it'd be helpful.

01:38:49.040 --> 01:38:53.090
Potentially theoretically
helpful in anorexics, of which,

01:38:53.090 --> 01:38:55.708
the incidence of anorexia in
men is increasing significantly.

01:38:55.708 --> 01:38:57.500
ANDREW HUBERMAN: As
you're telling me this,

01:38:57.500 --> 01:38:59.930
I'm remembering being
14 or 15 years old,

01:38:59.930 --> 01:39:02.210
and I would go into
the kitchen sometimes,

01:39:02.210 --> 01:39:05.690
and I was so hungry I would
just obliterate all the food.

01:39:05.690 --> 01:39:06.890
And I do remember being--

01:39:06.890 --> 01:39:08.640
I've always been a
pretty high energy guy,

01:39:08.640 --> 01:39:10.530
but having an immense
amount of energy.

01:39:10.530 --> 01:39:12.680
I can't recall if it was
a hangry feeling or not,

01:39:12.680 --> 01:39:14.388
but I'm guessing that
was growth hormone.

01:39:14.388 --> 01:39:16.430
I grew one foot in a
single academic year,

01:39:16.430 --> 01:39:20.450
so I imagine that was at least
in part due to growth hormone.

01:39:20.450 --> 01:39:23.450
In any case, sermorelin
is the peptide

01:39:23.450 --> 01:39:25.490
that I hear most often about.

01:39:25.490 --> 01:39:27.860
I admittedly tried a run of it.

01:39:27.860 --> 01:39:30.620
I was researching
a book, and decided

01:39:30.620 --> 01:39:33.260
to take it before sleep
on an empty stomach.

01:39:33.260 --> 01:39:37.710
It gave me a tremendous
depth of sleep,

01:39:37.710 --> 01:39:39.650
but that sleep was
really truncated,

01:39:39.650 --> 01:39:42.290
which is just nerd speak for
saying deep but short sleep.

01:39:42.290 --> 01:39:44.510
I would wake up after
very intense dreams.

01:39:44.510 --> 01:39:46.980
I can't say that it helped
me recover from exercise that

01:39:46.980 --> 01:39:47.480
much.

01:39:47.480 --> 01:39:50.210
I didn't notice any additional
fat loss or anything.

01:39:50.210 --> 01:39:52.515
Sort of abandoned it
except for occasional use.

01:39:52.515 --> 01:39:54.140
Again, this was
prescribed by a doctor.

01:39:56.960 --> 01:39:59.120
I'm starting to get the
sense that these peptides

01:39:59.120 --> 01:40:01.430
and their effects are somewhat
vague, and distributed,

01:40:01.430 --> 01:40:02.690
and highly individual.

01:40:02.690 --> 01:40:05.150
Is that a fair way
to describe them?

01:40:05.150 --> 01:40:07.130
KYLE GILLETT: Part
of the problem

01:40:07.130 --> 01:40:10.250
with the effect of peptides
is many people take them

01:40:10.250 --> 01:40:15.200
and levels that are far
above the physiologic range.

01:40:15.200 --> 01:40:18.710
Even individuals who are
checking their IGF-1 while they

01:40:18.710 --> 01:40:22.910
take these different
GHRPs, most of them

01:40:22.910 --> 01:40:25.910
do not check the binding
peptides-- for example,

01:40:25.910 --> 01:40:29.060
IGF binding peptide 1, 2, or 3.

01:40:29.060 --> 01:40:33.810
And their free IGF-1 level might
be significantly different.

01:40:33.810 --> 01:40:38.780
So common doses that people
will take these off-label

01:40:38.780 --> 01:40:42.380
for as a supplement
are often much greater

01:40:42.380 --> 01:40:44.745
than the therapeutic
or physiologic range.

01:40:44.745 --> 01:40:47.120
ANDREW HUBERMAN: Which, for
me, just underscores the fact

01:40:47.120 --> 01:40:48.287
that it's pretty precarious.

01:40:48.287 --> 01:40:50.660
I mean, I'm not coming in
here as the referee of what

01:40:50.660 --> 01:40:52.430
anyone should or shouldn't do.

01:40:52.430 --> 01:40:55.100
I'm just trying to gather
and distribute information.

01:40:55.100 --> 01:40:58.280
But I've heard, for instance,
that some companies where

01:40:58.280 --> 01:41:00.740
people can acquire these
things without prescription,

01:41:00.740 --> 01:41:03.170
those companies are not
good at cleaning out

01:41:03.170 --> 01:41:06.050
the lipopolysaccharide--
the LPS--

01:41:06.050 --> 01:41:08.120
which can cause an
inflammatory response.

01:41:08.120 --> 01:41:10.730
In other words, these
are dirty compounds.

01:41:10.730 --> 01:41:12.980
And that just sounds risky.

01:41:12.980 --> 01:41:15.110
It just sounds--
frankly, it just

01:41:15.110 --> 01:41:16.610
sounds really dangerous to me.

01:41:16.610 --> 01:41:20.540
KYLE GILLETT: LPS is a common
additive in many companies

01:41:20.540 --> 01:41:23.690
that are not
pharmacies, but they're

01:41:23.690 --> 01:41:26.930
selling things that people
often use as human consumption.

01:41:26.930 --> 01:41:29.450
One interesting note
about lipopolysaccharide

01:41:29.450 --> 01:41:32.850
is your gut microbiome actually
makes a lot of it as well,

01:41:32.850 --> 01:41:36.740
especially prevotella which
is a specific species, that

01:41:36.740 --> 01:41:40.470
can have to do with your
baseline body temperature.

01:41:40.470 --> 01:41:42.260
So your baseline
body temperature

01:41:42.260 --> 01:41:45.680
might also change depending
on if you're on a peptide that

01:41:45.680 --> 01:41:46.890
has LPS in it.

01:41:46.890 --> 01:41:49.400
ANDREW HUBERMAN: Yikes,
yikes, and yikes.

01:41:49.400 --> 01:41:52.400
[CHUCKLES] But I tend to
be pretty conservative

01:41:52.400 --> 01:41:54.410
when it comes to taking
anything exogenous.

01:41:54.410 --> 01:41:56.150
But I do rely on many
of the supplements

01:41:56.150 --> 01:41:58.400
that we talked about earlier
and I do try and optimize

01:41:58.400 --> 01:42:00.800
the behavioral things
and nutritional things

01:42:00.800 --> 01:42:02.300
for a long time.

01:42:02.300 --> 01:42:07.040
So then leaving
peptides behind, we

01:42:07.040 --> 01:42:10.140
are now I suppose in the
territory of exogenous hormone.

01:42:10.140 --> 01:42:13.358
So let's say that
somebody decides

01:42:13.358 --> 01:42:14.900
they're not concerned
with fertility,

01:42:14.900 --> 01:42:17.750
or they're going to bank sperm,
or they already have kids,

01:42:17.750 --> 01:42:19.910
or they're going to defer
on this issue of wanting

01:42:19.910 --> 01:42:22.220
to have kids, my
understanding is

01:42:22.220 --> 01:42:24.823
that nowadays, a lot of people
are using testosterone--

01:42:24.823 --> 01:42:26.240
let's not even
call it replacement

01:42:26.240 --> 01:42:29.330
therapy, because some of
these people have 600, 700,

01:42:29.330 --> 01:42:32.210
or even 800 nanogram
per deciliter read.

01:42:32.210 --> 01:42:34.832
So they're not replacing
anything that is diminished.

01:42:34.832 --> 01:42:37.040
They're just trying to
augment what's already there--

01:42:37.040 --> 01:42:38.460
increase what's already there.

01:42:38.460 --> 01:42:42.140
My understanding is that taking
a low dose more frequently

01:42:42.140 --> 01:42:45.020
is going to be more beneficial
than the kind of old school

01:42:45.020 --> 01:42:48.110
way of giving 100 or
even 200 milligrams

01:42:48.110 --> 01:42:50.287
in a single injection
once every two weeks.

01:42:50.287 --> 01:42:50.870
Is that right?

01:42:50.870 --> 01:42:52.513
And what do you do
with your patients?

01:42:52.513 --> 01:42:53.930
So let me give you
a hypothetical.

01:42:53.930 --> 01:42:57.680
Somebody comes into your office,
they do their blood work,

01:42:57.680 --> 01:43:01.160
and they have blood
levels of, let's say,

01:43:01.160 --> 01:43:03.650
600 nanogram per
deciliter testosterone.

01:43:03.650 --> 01:43:06.140
Their estrogen is
also in normal range.

01:43:06.140 --> 01:43:08.120
Everything else checks
out, but they're

01:43:08.120 --> 01:43:11.360
complaining of slightly
diminished libido, slightly

01:43:11.360 --> 01:43:15.700
poor recovery from workouts,
maybe reduced motivation

01:43:15.700 --> 01:43:17.620
and drive, although
no major depression.

01:43:17.620 --> 01:43:20.950
And you come to the conclusion
that testosterone therapy--

01:43:20.950 --> 01:43:22.960
not replacement, but
testosterone therapy

01:43:22.960 --> 01:43:24.430
might be a good
option to explore.

01:43:24.430 --> 01:43:28.030
What's a typical dosage
range and frequency

01:43:28.030 --> 01:43:32.517
of administration range that
you might consider exploring?

01:43:32.517 --> 01:43:34.600
KYLE GILLETT: And some of
this depends on the SHBG

01:43:34.600 --> 01:43:36.050
and free testosterone as well.

01:43:36.050 --> 01:43:39.310
So if that same individual had
a very high SHBG which, again,

01:43:39.310 --> 01:43:40.930
is the binding
protein that binds up

01:43:40.930 --> 01:43:43.750
the testosterone and all
androgens and estrogens,

01:43:43.750 --> 01:43:45.790
if it is extremely
high and they have

01:43:45.790 --> 01:43:48.910
a free testosterone
of two, then they

01:43:48.910 --> 01:43:50.740
might need a different
dose because they

01:43:50.740 --> 01:43:52.420
need enough
testosterone in order

01:43:52.420 --> 01:43:57.910
to have a normal eugonadal
free testosterone.

01:43:57.910 --> 01:44:01.090
But a general normal dosing
range, especially for someone

01:44:01.090 --> 01:44:04.930
starting, is around
100 to 120 milligrams

01:44:04.930 --> 01:44:08.080
divided over the course
of a week, usually

01:44:08.080 --> 01:44:11.230
either every other day or three
times a week-- occasionally,

01:44:11.230 --> 01:44:12.280
twice a week.

01:44:12.280 --> 01:44:15.140
Many people with
SHBG a bit higher

01:44:15.140 --> 01:44:17.380
can get away pretty
easily with twice a week.

01:44:17.380 --> 01:44:20.590
This is assuming that the ester
is cypionate or enanthate.

01:44:20.590 --> 01:44:23.230
ANDREW HUBERMAN: So two
60 milligram injections

01:44:23.230 --> 01:44:24.815
of testosterone
cypionate per week.

01:44:24.815 --> 01:44:26.440
KYLE GILLETT: Yeah,
very common dosing.

01:44:26.440 --> 01:44:28.607
ANDREW HUBERMAN: To hit
that 120 milligrams per week

01:44:28.607 --> 01:44:29.920
is kind of the typical average.

01:44:29.920 --> 01:44:30.837
KYLE GILLETT: Correct.

01:44:30.837 --> 01:44:34.300
And I would consider this like
a physiologic eugonadal dose.

01:44:34.300 --> 01:44:37.420
For many people, even
200 milligrams a week

01:44:37.420 --> 01:44:39.970
is far above the
reference range.

01:44:39.970 --> 01:44:41.710
All of this is said
with the caveat

01:44:41.710 --> 01:44:45.890
that testosterone is normally
released in a pulsatile manner.

01:44:45.890 --> 01:44:47.920
So it's high in the
morning, low in the evening.

01:44:47.920 --> 01:44:51.220
Whereas if you're on
testosterone therapy,

01:44:51.220 --> 01:44:54.832
then you're going to
have a steady state.

01:44:54.832 --> 01:44:56.290
So your testosterone
level is going

01:44:56.290 --> 01:44:59.560
to be pretty much the
same even in the evening.

01:44:59.560 --> 01:45:01.880
ANDREW HUBERMAN: And
in your experience,

01:45:01.880 --> 01:45:03.860
when patients do
that, I'm guessing

01:45:03.860 --> 01:45:05.540
they report that
normal constellation

01:45:05.540 --> 01:45:06.710
of positive effects--

01:45:06.710 --> 01:45:09.740
improved mood, improved energy,
improve sleep, recovery,

01:45:09.740 --> 01:45:10.910
et cetera.

01:45:10.910 --> 01:45:13.670
What are some of the
hazards or things that

01:45:13.670 --> 01:45:16.370
can crop up in bloodwork
or just subjectively

01:45:16.370 --> 01:45:19.910
that can be warning signs
that even a dosage of 120

01:45:19.910 --> 01:45:22.970
milligrams divided into these
two or three dosages per week

01:45:22.970 --> 01:45:24.500
is too high?

01:45:24.500 --> 01:45:26.430
KYLE GILLETT: Every
organ system in the body.

01:45:26.430 --> 01:45:29.330
So this is when you
really have to be

01:45:29.330 --> 01:45:33.560
at least well-versed in
every organ system, not just

01:45:33.560 --> 01:45:37.670
the gonadal genital system.

01:45:37.670 --> 01:45:41.840
You need to have
dermatology prowess.

01:45:41.840 --> 01:45:44.060
Acne is very common change.

01:45:44.060 --> 01:45:47.540
Lots of different skin
pathologies or even bruising

01:45:47.540 --> 01:45:49.640
can be related to
hormone replacement.

01:45:49.640 --> 01:45:52.730
Hair loss is very
common to see as well.

01:45:52.730 --> 01:45:54.350
Mental status changes.

01:45:54.350 --> 01:45:56.270
It could occasionally
even induce

01:45:56.270 --> 01:45:59.630
as a manic or a bipolar episode
because testosterone is also

01:45:59.630 --> 01:46:01.010
dopaminergic.

01:46:01.010 --> 01:46:04.010
And then a cardiovascularly
not just in the heart,

01:46:04.010 --> 01:46:07.610
but also concerns for like
microvascular ischemic disease.

01:46:07.610 --> 01:46:11.220
Ferritin buildup because
the estrogen also increases.

01:46:11.220 --> 01:46:15.740
And then fertility concerns as
well and lipid concerns too.

01:46:15.740 --> 01:46:18.800
So you really have to be
hematologist, dermatologist,

01:46:18.800 --> 01:46:23.600
cardiologist, lipidologist,
the whole 9 yards.

01:46:23.600 --> 01:46:25.730
ANDREW HUBERMAN:
So another reason--

01:46:25.730 --> 01:46:29.450
or set of reasons
rather to, if one

01:46:29.450 --> 01:46:31.430
is considering using
testosterone therapy,

01:46:31.430 --> 01:46:33.980
to really do this in
close communication

01:46:33.980 --> 01:46:36.110
with a really good
physician because that's

01:46:36.110 --> 01:46:36.818
a lot to monitor.

01:46:36.818 --> 01:46:39.193
Knowing whether or not you
have acne or not is one thing,

01:46:39.193 --> 01:46:41.202
but knowing whether or
not your LDL is going up,

01:46:41.202 --> 01:46:43.160
your ApoB is going up,
that's a whole other biz

01:46:43.160 --> 01:46:44.952
and that needs to be
done through bloodwork

01:46:44.952 --> 01:46:45.813
is what I'm hearing.

01:46:45.813 --> 01:46:46.730
KYLE GILLETT: Correct.

01:46:46.730 --> 01:46:50.000
And if your physician that
is managing or prescribing

01:46:50.000 --> 01:46:53.960
your testosterone
therapy or your HRT

01:46:53.960 --> 01:46:56.030
is not well-versed
in these systems,

01:46:56.030 --> 01:46:57.830
you would want him
or her to be part

01:46:57.830 --> 01:46:59.510
of an interdisciplinary
team where

01:46:59.510 --> 01:47:03.057
they have other experts that
can monitor those systems.

01:47:03.057 --> 01:47:04.640
ANDREW HUBERMAN: I
skipped over a sort

01:47:04.640 --> 01:47:08.300
of still intermediate set of
things-- prescription drugs--

01:47:08.300 --> 01:47:10.520
but maybe talking
about testosterone

01:47:10.520 --> 01:47:12.200
first was a bit of
a mistake on my part

01:47:12.200 --> 01:47:14.722
because I'm aware that
there are-- actually,

01:47:14.722 --> 01:47:17.180
I think there are companies,
but certainly groups out there

01:47:17.180 --> 01:47:20.780
that say, no, wait-- don't
go straight from nothing

01:47:20.780 --> 01:47:22.160
to supplements to testosterone.

01:47:22.160 --> 01:47:24.590
Once you're doing
behaviors and optimizing

01:47:24.590 --> 01:47:26.240
nutrition supplements--

01:47:26.240 --> 01:47:28.430
let's forget peptides--
instead of going straight

01:47:28.430 --> 01:47:32.180
to testosterone therapy, one
idea that many people are

01:47:32.180 --> 01:47:36.530
pursuing is to take the
prescription drugs that trigger

01:47:36.530 --> 01:47:39.050
luteinizing hormones--
so taking hCG--

01:47:39.050 --> 01:47:43.100
human chorionic gonadotropin,
which my understanding is

01:47:43.100 --> 01:47:45.260
will increase testosterone,
but also estrogen.

01:47:45.260 --> 01:47:47.475
Or they'll take things
like clomiphene.

01:47:47.475 --> 01:47:49.850
In fact, I think there are a
bunch of companies out there

01:47:49.850 --> 01:47:52.550
now that are saying don't take
testosterone-- it shuts down

01:47:52.550 --> 01:47:55.610
spermatogenesis, it shuts
down testosterone production--

01:47:55.610 --> 01:47:57.780
clomiphene is the way to go.

01:47:57.780 --> 01:48:01.135
Maybe you could educate us
about the hCG monotherapy,

01:48:01.135 --> 01:48:03.260
I think it's called, where
you're just mono-- one--

01:48:03.260 --> 01:48:07.490
just taking hCG and
clomiphene as a--

01:48:07.490 --> 01:48:12.633
and/or clomiphene as a tool
to ratchet up hormones.

01:48:12.633 --> 01:48:14.300
KYLE GILLETT: So a
quick points on hCG--

01:48:14.300 --> 01:48:16.790
human chorionic
gonadotropin-- made

01:48:16.790 --> 01:48:19.160
during especially the first
trimester of pregnancy,

01:48:19.160 --> 01:48:22.970
it has effects other than
binding to the LH receptor.

01:48:22.970 --> 01:48:25.952
It also binds to the TSH
receptor in the thyroid.

01:48:25.952 --> 01:48:28.160
ANDREW HUBERMAN: So it's
thyroid stimulating hormone?

01:48:28.160 --> 01:48:28.910
KYLE GILLETT: Yes.

01:48:28.910 --> 01:48:32.270
In fact, if you look at a
molecule of hCG and thyroid

01:48:32.270 --> 01:48:35.970
stimulating hormone, they
are extremely similar.

01:48:35.970 --> 01:48:38.810
However, you need a
relatively high dose of hCG

01:48:38.810 --> 01:48:40.590
to bind to the TSH receptor.

01:48:40.590 --> 01:48:42.710
This is the normal
mechanism in pregnancy

01:48:42.710 --> 01:48:46.010
that accounts for the increased
need of thyroid hormone--

01:48:46.010 --> 01:48:48.090
usually, about 30% to 40%.

01:48:48.090 --> 01:48:50.510
So that's why if someone
has hypothyroidism,

01:48:50.510 --> 01:48:52.190
you increase their
dose of thyroid,

01:48:52.190 --> 01:48:55.880
because the hCG is not going
to be doing it for you.

01:48:55.880 --> 01:49:00.050
The Clomid, or clomiphene,
there's two main--

01:49:00.050 --> 01:49:02.360
I believe it's diastereomers.

01:49:02.360 --> 01:49:04.430
And one of them is
enclomiphene and one of them

01:49:04.430 --> 01:49:06.320
is zuclomiphene.

01:49:06.320 --> 01:49:08.990
And these two work
slightly differently.

01:49:08.990 --> 01:49:12.560
Enclomiphene, I believe,
has a faster half life

01:49:12.560 --> 01:49:16.740
and it is potentially
slightly better tolerated.

01:49:16.740 --> 01:49:19.840
However, they were studying it--

01:49:19.840 --> 01:49:21.590
Clomid is a very
commonly prescribed drug,

01:49:21.590 --> 01:49:26.240
and obviously, there is plenty
of enclomiphene in Clomid.

01:49:26.240 --> 01:49:29.210
However, the drug which
was Andrew androxal--

01:49:29.210 --> 01:49:33.290
A-N-D-R-O-X-A-L-- did not go
all the way through the FDA

01:49:33.290 --> 01:49:35.743
approval process despite
Clomid being FDA approved.

01:49:35.743 --> 01:49:37.160
ANDREW HUBERMAN:
So there's Clomid

01:49:37.160 --> 01:49:40.280
which contains clomiphene,
but there are also--

01:49:40.280 --> 01:49:42.980
because we're talking about
male hormone optimization

01:49:42.980 --> 01:49:45.560
this episode-- there
are males out there

01:49:45.560 --> 01:49:48.410
who want to increase their
testosterone and other

01:49:48.410 --> 01:49:52.940
hormones-- maybe growth hormone,
et cetera-- who opt to not take

01:49:52.940 --> 01:49:56.720
exogenous testosterone-- so
no cream, no pellet, no pill,

01:49:56.720 --> 01:50:00.950
no injectable cypionate--
but decide to take clomiphene

01:50:00.950 --> 01:50:03.093
a couple of times a week.

01:50:03.093 --> 01:50:04.760
My understanding--
I've never done this.

01:50:04.760 --> 01:50:05.750
I would say if I had.

01:50:05.750 --> 01:50:09.110
My understanding is
that taking clomiphene--

01:50:09.110 --> 01:50:11.930
maybe two 50 milligram
tablets a week

01:50:11.930 --> 01:50:13.370
is what I hear
people are doing--

01:50:13.370 --> 01:50:17.570
will increase what--
luteinizing hormone,

01:50:17.570 --> 01:50:19.520
the various estrogen
receptor subunits?

01:50:19.520 --> 01:50:22.010
Could you explain how
clomiphene would benefit anyone,

01:50:22.010 --> 01:50:23.270
and is this a good strategy?

01:50:23.270 --> 01:50:26.060
I'm hearing that it's
being done quite a lot now.

01:50:26.060 --> 01:50:28.010
KYLE GILLETT: It will
increase testosterone

01:50:28.010 --> 01:50:30.260
in a dose dependent
manner, but it

01:50:30.260 --> 01:50:32.810
has many other
pharmacodynamic effects, which

01:50:32.810 --> 01:50:34.970
is the effect of
the drug on the body

01:50:34.970 --> 01:50:38.130
other than its effect on the
hypothalamus and the pituitary.

01:50:38.130 --> 01:50:40.680
So in the hypothalamus
and the pituitary,

01:50:40.680 --> 01:50:46.850
it does what's called negative
feedback inhibition or it

01:50:46.850 --> 01:50:50.600
blocks the action of estrogen.
So it crowds out estrogen

01:50:50.600 --> 01:50:53.990
from the estrogen receptor
on the hypothalamus

01:50:53.990 --> 01:50:54.980
and the pituitary.

01:50:54.980 --> 01:50:56.480
ANDREW HUBERMAN: And what's
this objective effect

01:50:56.480 --> 01:50:57.188
that would cause?

01:50:57.188 --> 01:51:00.170
So to my understanding
and experience of estrogen

01:51:00.170 --> 01:51:02.360
is that if I ever
took-- and I did

01:51:02.360 --> 01:51:04.610
take a very low dose of an
aromatase inhibitor once

01:51:04.610 --> 01:51:05.840
and I felt terrible.

01:51:05.840 --> 01:51:09.080
Actually reduced libido,
joints felt achy.

01:51:09.080 --> 01:51:11.540
That's when I discovered that,
wow, estrogen is actually

01:51:11.540 --> 01:51:14.720
really important for your brain
function, for joint function,

01:51:14.720 --> 01:51:16.040
and for libido.

01:51:16.040 --> 01:51:18.260
And suppressing
estrogen, for me, it just

01:51:18.260 --> 01:51:19.970
turned out to be the wrong idea.

01:51:19.970 --> 01:51:23.450
But my levels indicate that
it's within reference range.

01:51:23.450 --> 01:51:26.300
So why would I want
to take something

01:51:26.300 --> 01:51:30.200
that would increase the activity
of an estrogen receptor?

01:51:30.200 --> 01:51:32.960
I just can't find the
rationale for that.

01:51:32.960 --> 01:51:35.120
KYLE GILLETT: The main
rationale behind taking

01:51:35.120 --> 01:51:39.680
a serm is as a very
temporary measure that is not

01:51:39.680 --> 01:51:43.190
going to suppress pituitary
or hypothalamic function

01:51:43.190 --> 01:51:47.270
if your testosterone is just
so drastically low that it

01:51:47.270 --> 01:51:50.270
is unlikely to recover anyway.

01:51:50.270 --> 01:51:53.870
So most of the time it
is not clinically useful,

01:51:53.870 --> 01:51:56.810
and serm should
not be prescribed

01:51:56.810 --> 01:52:00.200
very often, certainly not
as long term testosterone

01:52:00.200 --> 01:52:03.830
replacement or testosterone
optimization in most

01:52:03.830 --> 01:52:04.340
individuals.

01:52:04.340 --> 01:52:06.560
There's always
exceptions to everything.

01:52:06.560 --> 01:52:10.040
But there's five
different estrogen

01:52:10.040 --> 01:52:12.140
and estrogen-related receptors.

01:52:12.140 --> 01:52:14.720
There's two main
estrogen receptors.

01:52:14.720 --> 01:52:19.250
And clomid and every serm
has a very unique profile

01:52:19.250 --> 01:52:23.090
because they selectively inhibit
some receptors in some tissues,

01:52:23.090 --> 01:52:25.250
but not other receptors
in other tissues.

01:52:25.250 --> 01:52:29.870
For example, Clomid can inhibit
receptors that are in the eye,

01:52:29.870 --> 01:52:35.390
and it can cause visual changes,
blurry vision, especially

01:52:35.390 --> 01:52:37.100
at higher doses.

01:52:37.100 --> 01:52:40.650
And it also acts in every
other tissue of the body.

01:52:40.650 --> 01:52:44.930
So a side effects from Clomid
and other selective estrogen

01:52:44.930 --> 01:52:48.103
receptor modifiers
are very common.

01:52:48.103 --> 01:52:49.520
ANDREW HUBERMAN:
So I'm at least--

01:52:49.520 --> 01:52:52.280
by my mind, I'm going to
pool them with peptides

01:52:52.280 --> 01:52:55.310
and say it sounds precarious
and probably not ideal

01:52:55.310 --> 01:52:56.930
for most people.

01:52:56.930 --> 01:52:59.930
Going back to testosterone
therapy then-- and notice,

01:52:59.930 --> 01:53:01.640
folks, I've deleted
the replacement part

01:53:01.640 --> 01:53:05.720
because I think so many people
are using testosterone therapy

01:53:05.720 --> 01:53:09.230
without the need to-- the
sort of reference range

01:53:09.230 --> 01:53:13.438
need to replace
anything, but rather are

01:53:13.438 --> 01:53:15.980
building on what they already
have for purposes of increasing

01:53:15.980 --> 01:53:17.660
vitality, et cetera.

01:53:17.660 --> 01:53:19.820
Going back to that,
my understanding

01:53:19.820 --> 01:53:23.450
is that taking hCG
several times per week

01:53:23.450 --> 01:53:25.820
can help maintain
spermatogenesis and fertility

01:53:25.820 --> 01:53:27.470
even while people
are on testosterone.

01:53:27.470 --> 01:53:29.330
But-- and you and I were
talking about this earlier--

01:53:29.330 --> 01:53:30.890
that there's
tremendous variation.

01:53:30.890 --> 01:53:33.500
Some people will take a
small amount testosterone

01:53:33.500 --> 01:53:35.460
and just crush
their sperm count.

01:53:35.460 --> 01:53:37.220
They just won't make
any viable sperm.

01:53:37.220 --> 01:53:39.800
Other people can maintain
viable sperm production

01:53:39.800 --> 01:53:41.600
while on testosterone,
especially

01:53:41.600 --> 01:53:43.340
if they're taking hCG.

01:53:43.340 --> 01:53:44.120
Is that right?

01:53:44.120 --> 01:53:44.750
KYLE GILLETT: Correct.

01:53:44.750 --> 01:53:46.167
And there's many
reasons for this.

01:53:46.167 --> 01:53:49.290
Some of this has to do with
heat damage to the testes,

01:53:49.290 --> 01:53:52.680
so potentially cold therapy
could be helpful for that.

01:53:52.680 --> 01:53:53.180
And--

01:53:53.180 --> 01:53:54.320
ANDREW HUBERMAN: Ice
baths, cold showers?

01:53:54.320 --> 01:53:55.175
KYLE GILLETT: Mhm.

01:53:55.175 --> 01:53:56.210
ANDREW HUBERMAN:
Yeah, or just avoid--

01:53:56.210 --> 01:53:57.590
and certainly avoiding--

01:53:57.590 --> 01:53:58.280
KYLE GILLETT: Mostly
avoiding heat.

01:53:58.280 --> 01:53:58.850
ANDREW HUBERMAN:
--sauna and hot tub.

01:53:58.850 --> 01:53:59.823
Yeah.

01:53:59.823 --> 01:54:01.490
KYLE GILLETT: Stopping
the daily hot tub

01:54:01.490 --> 01:54:03.440
can restore fertility
in many people.

01:54:03.440 --> 01:54:05.210
ANDREW HUBERMAN: I
know a number of people

01:54:05.210 --> 01:54:07.400
that are trying to
conceive children that

01:54:07.400 --> 01:54:09.590
go into the sauna,
and they'll just

01:54:09.590 --> 01:54:12.215
put a cold pack in their shorts
or between their legs depending

01:54:12.215 --> 01:54:14.173
on whether or not they're
wearing shorts or not

01:54:14.173 --> 01:54:15.200
when they go in.

01:54:15.200 --> 01:54:16.880
Or they'll alternate
ice and heat

01:54:16.880 --> 01:54:22.400
in a way that maintains
coolness of the milieu

01:54:22.400 --> 01:54:24.480
in which the sperm live.

01:54:24.480 --> 01:54:28.310
In other words, they're cooling
their scrotum deliberately

01:54:28.310 --> 01:54:30.800
in order to avoid
killing the sperm.

01:54:30.800 --> 01:54:32.720
Actually, I saw an
interesting paper

01:54:32.720 --> 01:54:38.450
that said that for every two
degree increase in temperature

01:54:38.450 --> 01:54:42.260
of the scrotum, there's a 20%
decrease in spermatogenesis

01:54:42.260 --> 01:54:44.420
and viability of sperm.

01:54:44.420 --> 01:54:46.760
And that actually, if you
look at the difference

01:54:46.760 --> 01:54:49.160
between people who
stand a lot, sit a lot,

01:54:49.160 --> 01:54:52.490
and drive a lot, what you see is
a progressive decrease in sperm

01:54:52.490 --> 01:54:54.122
count because when
people are sitting,

01:54:54.122 --> 01:54:55.580
there's an increase
in temperature,

01:54:55.580 --> 01:54:57.990
and then when they're sitting
on the hot seat of the car,

01:54:57.990 --> 01:55:00.530
there's an-- or using
the heated seats,

01:55:00.530 --> 01:55:01.640
actually, it kills sperm.

01:55:01.640 --> 01:55:03.260
I think there are
good data on that.

01:55:03.260 --> 01:55:04.718
KYLE GILLETT: Yeah,
excellent data,

01:55:04.718 --> 01:55:06.600
and anecdotally,
you see it as well.

01:55:06.600 --> 01:55:10.610
I've had several patients come
in for fertility consultations.

01:55:10.610 --> 01:55:14.060
And all we do is like, no
medications, no supplements.

01:55:14.060 --> 01:55:18.740
We change their--
several lifestyle things.

01:55:18.740 --> 01:55:20.960
Very tight fitting
clothing is another one.

01:55:20.960 --> 01:55:25.010
And soon, they have fertility
again and they're no longer--

01:55:25.010 --> 01:55:28.580
they have sperm whereas
before, they did not.

01:55:28.580 --> 01:55:30.740
ANDREW HUBERMAN: Interesting.

01:55:30.740 --> 01:55:33.897
I'd like to talk about some
of the do's and don'ts, but we

01:55:33.897 --> 01:55:36.230
have talked about a lot of
do's-- things that one can do

01:55:36.230 --> 01:55:37.230
to optimize hormones.

01:55:37.230 --> 01:55:41.900
Maybe we could just do sort
of more rapid fire Q&amp;A on some

01:55:41.900 --> 01:55:45.920
of the don'ts and maybe throw
in some science where you feel

01:55:45.920 --> 01:55:47.750
it's appropriate.

01:55:47.750 --> 01:55:51.080
Cannabis, marijuana,
THC-- yes or no--

01:55:51.080 --> 01:55:55.050
it diminishes
testosterone levels?

01:55:55.050 --> 01:55:57.900
KYLE GILLETT: Smoked
cannabis, I would say,

01:55:57.900 --> 01:56:00.630
diminishes testosterone,
increases prolactin.

01:56:00.630 --> 01:56:01.530
That's a no.

01:56:01.530 --> 01:56:04.360
Other cannabinoids, not
particularly harmful.

01:56:04.360 --> 01:56:06.510
ANDREW HUBERMAN: So CBD?

01:56:06.510 --> 01:56:08.580
KYLE GILLETT: CBD, not
particularly harmful.

01:56:08.580 --> 01:56:11.190
Smoked CBD, I'm not sure.

01:56:11.190 --> 01:56:14.310
ANDREW HUBERMAN: What about
edible cannabis and THC?

01:56:14.310 --> 01:56:17.070
KYLE GILLETT: As far as I
know, edible cannabis and THC

01:56:17.070 --> 01:56:20.250
does not significantly
increase prolactin to a point

01:56:20.250 --> 01:56:23.520
where it would be
disruptive of hormones.

01:56:23.520 --> 01:56:26.172
ANDREW HUBERMAN: Can
marijuana, THC, cannabis,

01:56:26.172 --> 01:56:28.380
whatever you want to call
it, increase gynecomastia--

01:56:28.380 --> 01:56:29.910
the growth of male
breast tissue?

01:56:29.910 --> 01:56:31.590
KYLE GILLETT: Yes,
it certainly can,

01:56:31.590 --> 01:56:35.370
and there's a pretty good
association between smoked THC

01:56:35.370 --> 01:56:37.550
and gynecomastia.

01:56:37.550 --> 01:56:40.640
ANDREW HUBERMAN: What about
nicotine and testosterone

01:56:40.640 --> 01:56:44.490
and estrogen and other
hormones-- smoked nicotine?

01:56:44.490 --> 01:56:46.100
KYLE GILLETT: Nicotine
is particularly

01:56:46.100 --> 01:56:48.230
concerning not only for
testosterone, but also

01:56:48.230 --> 01:56:51.530
for estrogen. Part of it is, if
you're talking about nicotine

01:56:51.530 --> 01:56:53.930
from tobacco, there's many
other carcinogens in it,

01:56:53.930 --> 01:56:55.490
especially if it's smoked.

01:56:55.490 --> 01:56:57.740
But nicotine, even
if it is chewed

01:56:57.740 --> 01:56:59.340
in a dose dependent manner--

01:56:59.340 --> 01:57:02.750
so if you can use an extremely
small amount of nicotine,

01:57:02.750 --> 01:57:05.340
then it's not as
concerning in the long run.

01:57:05.340 --> 01:57:07.880
But it's a
vasoconstrictor, and one

01:57:07.880 --> 01:57:11.660
of the main concerns with it
would be cardiovascular disease

01:57:11.660 --> 01:57:16.100
or even microvascular
ischemic disease that

01:57:16.100 --> 01:57:18.300
can lead to
neurodegenerative disease,

01:57:18.300 --> 01:57:22.010
so like a type of dementia that
can be partly due to nicotine.

01:57:22.010 --> 01:57:25.860
If you use nicotine for a
very long period of time,

01:57:25.860 --> 01:57:28.280
especially at a
higher dose, it's

01:57:28.280 --> 01:57:32.180
a dose-dependent effect
on your hormone profile.

01:57:32.180 --> 01:57:34.180
ANDREW HUBERMAN: Is that
also true for Nicorette

01:57:34.180 --> 01:57:36.572
and other nicotine gums?

01:57:36.572 --> 01:57:38.030
KYLE GILLETT: At
high doses, if you

01:57:38.030 --> 01:57:42.650
can use an extremely low
dose of a nicotine gum,

01:57:42.650 --> 01:57:46.970
then theoretically, that
would be maintainable.

01:57:46.970 --> 01:57:50.330
It's not going to overload
the nicotinic receptor.

01:57:50.330 --> 01:57:53.150
You have acetylcholine
and the cholinergic system

01:57:53.150 --> 01:57:56.030
is one of your main
nervous systems, of course.

01:57:56.030 --> 01:57:57.650
And you have
muscarinic receptors

01:57:57.650 --> 01:58:00.020
and nicotinic receptors,
and there's just

01:58:00.020 --> 01:58:04.610
better ways to optimize your
nicotinic receptor activity.

01:58:04.610 --> 01:58:06.770
For example,
acetylcholine precursors

01:58:06.770 --> 01:58:09.230
like alpha GPC,
phosphatidylserine,

01:58:09.230 --> 01:58:11.420
phosphatidylcholine.

01:58:11.420 --> 01:58:13.400
Weak acetylcholinesterase
inhibitors,

01:58:13.400 --> 01:58:14.930
especially natural
ones, potentially

01:58:14.930 --> 01:58:17.130
have a part as well.

01:58:17.130 --> 01:58:18.650
And then other alkaloids.

01:58:18.650 --> 01:58:21.800
So nicotine is an alkaloid
from the tobacco plant.

01:58:21.800 --> 01:58:24.710
There are other
plants like cytosine

01:58:24.710 --> 01:58:28.850
and that genus of plants,
and that alkaloid is also

01:58:28.850 --> 01:58:33.050
a nicotine receptor agonist.

01:58:33.050 --> 01:58:36.350
ANDREW HUBERMAN: Is it true
that cycling for too long--

01:58:36.350 --> 01:58:39.440
literally, bicycling-- sitting
on a bike seat too long

01:58:39.440 --> 01:58:41.540
can damage the prostate?

01:58:41.540 --> 01:58:43.890
KYLE GILLETT: Yes, it
can be very concerning,

01:58:43.890 --> 01:58:46.880
especially if you're seated
while cycling, especially

01:58:46.880 --> 01:58:49.550
if you're putting a lot of
pressure on the perineum.

01:58:49.550 --> 01:58:52.730
Your core is kind
of like a box where

01:58:52.730 --> 01:58:56.300
your diaphragm sort of makes the
top and your abs and serratus

01:58:56.300 --> 01:58:58.400
make the front and the sides.

01:58:58.400 --> 01:59:01.760
Your back muscles make the
back, and then your pelvic floor

01:59:01.760 --> 01:59:03.680
makes the bottom
of the box, which

01:59:03.680 --> 01:59:06.740
is arguably the most
important part of your core.

01:59:06.740 --> 01:59:09.230
And that pressure
can weaken and even

01:59:09.230 --> 01:59:12.798
lead to incontinence
and impotence.

01:59:12.798 --> 01:59:14.840
ANDREW HUBERMAN: So we
were talking earlier today

01:59:14.840 --> 01:59:18.440
in the gym about how
heavy legwork, hack

01:59:18.440 --> 01:59:20.780
squats, deadlifts, those
kinds of things a lot of guys

01:59:20.780 --> 01:59:24.150
are doing to increase their
testosterone, done correctly,

01:59:24.150 --> 01:59:26.120
can actually
augment and build up

01:59:26.120 --> 01:59:27.590
the strength of
the pelvic floor.

01:59:27.590 --> 01:59:30.050
Done incorrectly, can actually
weaken the pelvic floor

01:59:30.050 --> 01:59:32.870
and lead to all sorts of issues,
including sexual effects--

01:59:32.870 --> 01:59:34.170
negative sexual effects.

01:59:34.170 --> 01:59:37.760
So how does one go about
learning whether or not

01:59:37.760 --> 01:59:39.590
their movements are
being done properly

01:59:39.590 --> 01:59:45.110
to support pelvic floor or
to destruct pelvic floor?

01:59:45.110 --> 01:59:47.210
KYLE GILLETT: The pelvic
floor is a constellation

01:59:47.210 --> 01:59:48.710
of muscles just
like any other kind

01:59:48.710 --> 01:59:50.360
of like system in the body.

01:59:50.360 --> 01:59:54.450
And form is important.

01:59:54.450 --> 01:59:57.540
If you're doing the valsalva
maneuver, which again,

01:59:57.540 --> 02:00:02.550
is that bearing down or deep
breath where you feel all

02:00:02.550 --> 02:00:04.290
of your abs are
tight, you can also

02:00:04.290 --> 02:00:07.440
notice that your pelvic
floor is tight as well.

02:00:07.440 --> 02:00:10.530
If you have a history of
an inguinal hernia, which

02:00:10.530 --> 02:00:13.950
is a hole kind of like
connecting the abdominal cavity

02:00:13.950 --> 02:00:15.750
down through the
pelvic floor or even

02:00:15.750 --> 02:00:17.280
the scrotum in some
cases-- and that

02:00:17.280 --> 02:00:21.570
can be a sign that there
is weakness in that area,

02:00:21.570 --> 02:00:23.070
and you might have
to concentrate it

02:00:23.070 --> 02:00:25.410
on it most, or even
have a physiotherapist

02:00:25.410 --> 02:00:28.020
or a physical
therapist specifically

02:00:28.020 --> 02:00:29.730
target the pelvic floor.

02:00:29.730 --> 02:00:33.300
Many exercises in which
you valsalva or use

02:00:33.300 --> 02:00:36.390
your glutes or
legs, you can learn

02:00:36.390 --> 02:00:39.870
to squeeze them and have that
mind-muscle connection in order

02:00:39.870 --> 02:00:41.520
to help build up
the pelvic floor.

02:00:41.520 --> 02:00:42.780
And there's other things.

02:00:42.780 --> 02:00:44.520
Many people are
familiar with kegels.

02:00:44.520 --> 02:00:47.400
That is just one of the
many different exercises

02:00:47.400 --> 02:00:49.080
that can help your pelvic floor.

02:00:49.080 --> 02:00:49.800
ANDREW HUBERMAN:
My understanding

02:00:49.800 --> 02:00:52.170
is that while strengthening
the pelvic floor is good,

02:00:52.170 --> 02:00:53.970
excessive contraction
of the pelvic floor

02:00:53.970 --> 02:00:56.730
can actually limit blood flow
to the pelvic area, the penis,

02:00:56.730 --> 02:00:57.430
and so forth.

02:00:57.430 --> 02:00:59.880
So this is, again, a
double-edged sword.

02:00:59.880 --> 02:01:01.620
I mean, you don't
want guys out there

02:01:01.620 --> 02:01:03.870
to just start doing endless
number of kegels every day

02:01:03.870 --> 02:01:05.662
because they're actually
going to constrict

02:01:05.662 --> 02:01:06.870
blood flow to that area.

02:01:06.870 --> 02:01:10.350
There's-- and in fact,
the erection response is

02:01:10.350 --> 02:01:11.340
parasympathetic.

02:01:11.340 --> 02:01:13.363
It's a relaxed induced
response, right?

02:01:13.363 --> 02:01:14.280
KYLE GILLETT: Correct.

02:01:14.280 --> 02:01:17.850
ANDREW HUBERMAN: So for the--
the reason I chuckle is that

02:01:17.850 --> 02:01:18.480
for--

02:01:18.480 --> 02:01:19.938
because we're
talking about things,

02:01:19.938 --> 02:01:22.440
we don't have visuals or
charts, and certainly, it's

02:01:22.440 --> 02:01:25.890
hard to know whether or not
a given exercise like kegels

02:01:25.890 --> 02:01:28.170
are going to be
good or not good.

02:01:28.170 --> 02:01:29.430
If it's excessive, what--

02:01:29.430 --> 02:01:32.700
how many sets and reps
does it take before it

02:01:32.700 --> 02:01:34.243
goes from good to bad.

02:01:34.243 --> 02:01:35.910
Is there a kind of
general rule of thumb

02:01:35.910 --> 02:01:37.202
for people to think about this?

02:01:37.202 --> 02:01:39.420
I mean, clearly blood
flow to that area

02:01:39.420 --> 02:01:42.180
is key for sexual performance.

02:01:42.180 --> 02:01:45.360
And yet when one trains
the legs or even walks,

02:01:45.360 --> 02:01:46.990
you're getting blood flow.

02:01:46.990 --> 02:01:50.670
So my understanding is this
that a combination of weight

02:01:50.670 --> 02:01:52.770
training to stimulate
the positive hormonal,

02:01:52.770 --> 02:01:55.380
and muscular, and
connective tissue growth

02:01:55.380 --> 02:01:58.050
is key provided it's
not overtraining,

02:01:58.050 --> 02:02:02.257
but so is casual exercise
like walking, and stretching,

02:02:02.257 --> 02:02:03.840
and the sorts of
things that will then

02:02:03.840 --> 02:02:05.460
return blood flow to that area.

02:02:05.460 --> 02:02:08.700
Is that an overly basic
way to think about it

02:02:08.700 --> 02:02:09.613
or will that suffice?

02:02:09.613 --> 02:02:12.030
KYLE GILLETT: I think that's
a good way to think about it.

02:02:12.030 --> 02:02:13.770
I think the main
point with kegels

02:02:13.770 --> 02:02:17.140
is they're just one of
many different things.

02:02:17.140 --> 02:02:19.800
So if you're having some
pelvic floor pathology

02:02:19.800 --> 02:02:22.920
certainly or even just concerned
about your pelvic floor,

02:02:22.920 --> 02:02:27.210
don't just take the advice
do kegels and you'll be OK.

02:02:27.210 --> 02:02:28.380
That is not near enough.

02:02:28.380 --> 02:02:31.570
It's just one of
the many aspects.

02:02:31.570 --> 02:02:33.570
ANDREW HUBERMAN: So going
back to the rapid Q&amp;A,

02:02:33.570 --> 02:02:35.250
and then we'll come back
to this issue of blood flow

02:02:35.250 --> 02:02:37.890
because there's some interesting
science and protocols there--

02:02:37.890 --> 02:02:40.710
the question I have
is, alcohol, does it

02:02:40.710 --> 02:02:44.010
increase aromatase, the enzyme
that converts testosterone

02:02:44.010 --> 02:02:45.420
into estrogen or not?

02:02:45.420 --> 02:02:48.450
And is there a dose
dependence there?

02:02:48.450 --> 02:02:49.950
KYLE GILLETT: It
significantly does.

02:02:49.950 --> 02:02:51.360
There is a dose dependence.

02:02:51.360 --> 02:02:55.860
In general, I would not
recommend more than three

02:02:55.860 --> 02:02:59.040
to four standard drinks.

02:02:59.040 --> 02:03:02.340
One huge glass of wine is
probably five standard drinks.

02:03:02.340 --> 02:03:06.947
But I'd say every two weeks.

02:03:06.947 --> 02:03:09.030
ANDREW HUBERMAN: Yeah,
that's consistent with what

02:03:09.030 --> 02:03:11.430
I discovered researching
alcohol in an episode we

02:03:11.430 --> 02:03:12.540
did on alcohol.

02:03:12.540 --> 02:03:16.665
That no alcohol is definitely
better for all aspects

02:03:16.665 --> 02:03:17.790
of health than any alcohol.

02:03:17.790 --> 02:03:19.890
And anyone that says that,
well, red wine contains

02:03:19.890 --> 02:03:21.685
these various things,
well, it doesn't

02:03:21.685 --> 02:03:23.310
contain enough of
those positive things

02:03:23.310 --> 02:03:24.393
to have a positive effect.

02:03:24.393 --> 02:03:27.150
But that if people do
opt to drink alcohol,

02:03:27.150 --> 02:03:29.220
that two drinks per week--

02:03:29.220 --> 02:03:34.470
and meaning 20 grams of alcohol,
so that's probably two 12 ounce

02:03:34.470 --> 02:03:37.410
beers or two 4 ounce
glasses of wine--

02:03:37.410 --> 02:03:39.660
is going to be the upper
limit beyond which you're

02:03:39.660 --> 02:03:42.100
going to start seeing all
sorts of negative effects.

02:03:42.100 --> 02:03:43.905
KYLE GILLETT: The other thing to
keep in mind with alcohol is it

02:03:43.905 --> 02:03:46.230
has a lot of calories--
seven kilocalories

02:03:46.230 --> 02:03:49.200
per gram, almost as
much as fat, which is 9.

02:03:49.200 --> 02:03:51.210
And then it's also
very GABAergic,

02:03:51.210 --> 02:03:55.890
so it can activate
inhibitory neurotransmission,

02:03:55.890 --> 02:04:02.580
and that can also affect how
much LH and FSH is released.

02:04:02.580 --> 02:04:04.890
So that can also
decrease testosterone

02:04:04.890 --> 02:04:08.580
almost kind of
similar to how opiates

02:04:08.580 --> 02:04:10.620
can decrease testosterone.

02:04:10.620 --> 02:04:13.350
ANDREW HUBERMAN: And I feel
very lucky that I don't enjoy

02:04:13.350 --> 02:04:14.710
alcohol-- never really did.

02:04:14.710 --> 02:04:16.230
I can kind of take
it or leave it.

02:04:16.230 --> 02:04:18.673
I certainly don't like sedatives
like Valium or anything

02:04:18.673 --> 02:04:20.340
like that, which, as
you just mentioned,

02:04:20.340 --> 02:04:22.770
can suppress testosterone.

02:04:22.770 --> 02:04:26.250
You said the word fat, so
I'm going to pick up on that

02:04:26.250 --> 02:04:29.190
and say, in order to
optimize hormone production,

02:04:29.190 --> 02:04:33.240
is it important to have some
saturated fat in one's diet?

02:04:33.240 --> 02:04:36.470
And what happens on very low
fat diets to testosterone,

02:04:36.470 --> 02:04:39.390
and estrogen, and
other steroid hormones?

02:04:39.390 --> 02:04:42.060
KYLE GILLETT: Fat is
interesting because there are so

02:04:42.060 --> 02:04:44.100
many different beneficial fats.

02:04:44.100 --> 02:04:48.000
Omega 3s-- almost every American
gets plenty of omega 6s--

02:04:48.000 --> 02:04:50.250
in any developed country really.

02:04:50.250 --> 02:04:53.240
When it comes to
saturated fat, there

02:04:53.240 --> 02:04:56.540
is more of a correlation
with hormone optimisation.

02:04:56.540 --> 02:04:58.790
If you're eating things
with saturated fat,

02:04:58.790 --> 02:05:00.050
you tend to have--

02:05:00.050 --> 02:05:03.680
those are things with more fat
soluble vitamins and things

02:05:03.680 --> 02:05:06.390
that are very nutrient
dense otherwise.

02:05:06.390 --> 02:05:07.730
But it is not vital.

02:05:07.730 --> 02:05:11.180
In general, you want to
eliminate any trans fat

02:05:11.180 --> 02:05:13.250
unless it's trans fat
from the ruminants.

02:05:13.250 --> 02:05:15.020
There's always an
exception to everything.

02:05:15.020 --> 02:05:18.020
So there are healthy
trans omega 3 fats, which

02:05:18.020 --> 02:05:20.180
are formed in the
stomach of grass fed

02:05:20.180 --> 02:05:23.220
and finished ruminants.

02:05:23.220 --> 02:05:26.400
ANDREW HUBERMAN: But
ingesting mostly olive oils,

02:05:26.400 --> 02:05:29.640
maybe nut butters in limited
amounts because they're

02:05:29.640 --> 02:05:31.193
very calorie dense, but--

02:05:31.193 --> 02:05:33.360
unless people are trying
to increase their calories,

02:05:33.360 --> 02:05:34.902
in which case,
they're a great source

02:05:34.902 --> 02:05:39.027
of calories, small amounts
of butter, ghee, probably OK,

02:05:39.027 --> 02:05:40.110
but not excessive amounts?

02:05:40.110 --> 02:05:40.920
Is that the idea?

02:05:40.920 --> 02:05:41.820
KYLE GILLETT: Yes.

02:05:41.820 --> 02:05:43.440
Fat is perfectly fine.

02:05:43.440 --> 02:05:47.490
Cholesterol has an interesting--
so cholesterol and, in general,

02:05:47.490 --> 02:05:51.420
phospholipids make the bilayer
that's around the cell.

02:05:51.420 --> 02:05:54.600
But cholesterol is also a
hormone in and of itself

02:05:54.600 --> 02:05:58.050
because it binds to the
estrogen-related receptor

02:05:58.050 --> 02:05:58.680
alpha.

02:05:58.680 --> 02:06:01.740
So I consider that like in the
estrogen receptor category,

02:06:01.740 --> 02:06:03.550
and that can help
with metabolism,

02:06:03.550 --> 02:06:05.760
but also potentially
have concerns

02:06:05.760 --> 02:06:08.627
for cancer and tumor risk.

02:06:08.627 --> 02:06:10.710
ANDREW HUBERMAN: I want
to go back to the prostate

02:06:10.710 --> 02:06:12.450
and talk to you about
something that's

02:06:12.450 --> 02:06:14.220
kind of a newer emerging trend.

02:06:14.220 --> 02:06:16.500
I know that you've talked
a little bit about this

02:06:16.500 --> 02:06:20.400
in previous podcasts, that a
number of men-- or I should say

02:06:20.400 --> 02:06:23.340
a number of physicians
are prescribing

02:06:23.340 --> 02:06:26.460
low dose tadalafil,
also known as Cialis,

02:06:26.460 --> 02:06:28.090
to their male patients.

02:06:28.090 --> 02:06:31.560
So in dosage ranges of like
2.5 milligrams to 5 milligrams

02:06:31.560 --> 02:06:33.600
per day, but not for
erectile dysfunction,

02:06:33.600 --> 02:06:36.060
but rather for improving
prostate health.

02:06:36.060 --> 02:06:39.690
And presumably, they get sort of
a boost in terms of blood flow

02:06:39.690 --> 02:06:41.230
to the genitalia as well.

02:06:41.230 --> 02:06:45.030
But again, not specifically to
deal with erectile dysfunction,

02:06:45.030 --> 02:06:49.080
but to deal with prostate health
and blood flow to the prostate.

02:06:49.080 --> 02:06:50.940
Is that something
that you sometimes--

02:06:50.940 --> 02:06:54.720
often prescribe to your
patients, and of what age?

02:06:54.720 --> 02:06:57.570
KYLE GILLETT: Tadalafil is a
very underrated medication.

02:06:57.570 --> 02:07:00.990
The age would kind of
depend on the indication.

02:07:00.990 --> 02:07:04.530
So tadalafil is also a
blood pressure medication.

02:07:04.530 --> 02:07:06.520
It can very slightly
decrease blood pressure,

02:07:06.520 --> 02:07:08.460
especially at higher doses.

02:07:08.460 --> 02:07:10.680
At higher doses, it--

02:07:10.680 --> 02:07:14.370
a high dose would be 20
milligrams, not 2.5 milligrams.

02:07:14.370 --> 02:07:16.680
But consistently,
it can somewhat

02:07:16.680 --> 02:07:19.020
affect with the cones
in the eye that have

02:07:19.020 --> 02:07:20.700
to do with red and green sight.

02:07:20.700 --> 02:07:23.260
Although, if you remove it,
that effect is reversed.

02:07:23.260 --> 02:07:26.100
So basically, if you don't need
really, really good red/green

02:07:26.100 --> 02:07:28.240
discrimination, you
can take higher doses.

02:07:28.240 --> 02:07:30.270
But in general, I
recommend no higher

02:07:30.270 --> 02:07:32.640
than 10 milligrams
a day-- usually just

02:07:32.640 --> 02:07:35.490
two or 5 milligrams.

02:07:35.490 --> 02:07:39.540
One other benefit or
other use of tadalafil

02:07:39.540 --> 02:07:42.780
is that it increases the
density of the androgen receptor

02:07:42.780 --> 02:07:45.660
similarly to l-carnitine.

02:07:45.660 --> 02:07:47.070
So that's an
interesting benefit.

02:07:47.070 --> 02:07:49.380
Another benefit is
that if you give it

02:07:49.380 --> 02:07:51.270
to people with
nocturia, which is

02:07:51.270 --> 02:07:53.030
urinating at night
in general, it

02:07:53.030 --> 02:07:54.820
will cut the episodes in half.

02:07:54.820 --> 02:07:57.210
So it could go
from 2 to 1, which

02:07:57.210 --> 02:07:59.280
can make a big difference
for your sleep, which

02:07:59.280 --> 02:08:01.530
will secondarily make a big
difference for your growth

02:08:01.530 --> 02:08:03.270
hormone and testosterone
optimization.

02:08:03.270 --> 02:08:04.478
ANDREW HUBERMAN: Interesting.

02:08:04.478 --> 02:08:06.330
So you said 2.5 to
5 milligrams per day

02:08:06.330 --> 02:08:09.120
is typical for these
prostate enhancing effects.

02:08:09.120 --> 02:08:10.152
KYLE GILLETT: Yes.

02:08:10.152 --> 02:08:12.360
ANDREW HUBERMAN: And you
mentioned the potential side

02:08:12.360 --> 02:08:14.280
effects on adjusting
visual perception.

02:08:14.280 --> 02:08:17.790
As a vision scientist,
that rings in my mind.

02:08:17.790 --> 02:08:20.317
But in terms of red/green
color discrimination,

02:08:20.317 --> 02:08:21.900
I'm guessing unless
you're going to be

02:08:21.900 --> 02:08:24.060
a subject in one of the
experiments in my lab

02:08:24.060 --> 02:08:25.608
or you want to be
a fighter pilot,

02:08:25.608 --> 02:08:27.150
chances are you can
probably get away

02:08:27.150 --> 02:08:29.233
with a little less red/green
color discrimination.

02:08:29.233 --> 02:08:30.150
KYLE GILLETT: Correct.

02:08:30.150 --> 02:08:32.070
It's not considered
clinically significant

02:08:32.070 --> 02:08:34.592
unless someone is
a commercial pilot.

02:08:34.592 --> 02:08:35.550
ANDREW HUBERMAN: Great.

02:08:35.550 --> 02:08:37.842
KYLE GILLETT: So if someone's
getting their pilot exam,

02:08:37.842 --> 02:08:39.547
that's one of the
things we look for.

02:08:39.547 --> 02:08:41.380
ANDREW HUBERMAN: So
commercial pilots aside,

02:08:41.380 --> 02:08:43.380
you might want to ask
your doctor about low dose

02:08:43.380 --> 02:08:46.770
tadalafil for sake of
enhancing prostate health.

02:08:46.770 --> 02:08:49.438
Certainly monitoring PSA
prostate specific antigen

02:08:49.438 --> 02:08:49.980
is important.

02:08:49.980 --> 02:08:52.140
I can give an anecdote there.

02:08:52.140 --> 02:08:55.830
When I tried sermorelin, one
of the surprising side effects

02:08:55.830 --> 02:08:59.250
that was not welcome
was a dramatic spike

02:08:59.250 --> 02:09:01.140
in my prostate specific
antigen. No one

02:09:01.140 --> 02:09:04.458
could explain to me
why that would happen,

02:09:04.458 --> 02:09:06.000
but when I stopped
taking sermorelin,

02:09:06.000 --> 02:09:07.210
it went back to normal.

02:09:07.210 --> 02:09:09.690
So that's one reason I
avoid sermorelin, at least,

02:09:09.690 --> 02:09:11.730
frequent use of sermorelin.

02:09:11.730 --> 02:09:14.070
PSA should be kept--
what-- below levels

02:09:14.070 --> 02:09:17.220
of somewhere between 1 and
4 is considered healthy?

02:09:17.220 --> 02:09:17.850
Is that right?

02:09:17.850 --> 02:09:19.350
KYLE GILLETT: It
depends on the age.

02:09:19.350 --> 02:09:22.350
If there's a 20-year-old,
likely between 0 and 1.

02:09:22.350 --> 02:09:26.922
If there's a 40-year-old,
likely between 1 and 3.

02:09:26.922 --> 02:09:28.380
And then if there's
an 80-year-old,

02:09:28.380 --> 02:09:31.170
it would not be abnormal
to have a PSA of 5

02:09:31.170 --> 02:09:34.112
and have that be well
within the reference range.

02:09:34.112 --> 02:09:35.820
Another thing we should
mention about PSA

02:09:35.820 --> 02:09:38.670
is if you do take a
5-alpha reductase inhibitor

02:09:38.670 --> 02:09:41.850
like finasteride or
dutasteride, often

02:09:41.850 --> 02:09:44.260
these will cut your PSA in half.

02:09:44.260 --> 02:09:47.820
So if you-- for example,
if you have a PSA of 6

02:09:47.820 --> 02:09:50.010
and you start finasteride
or dutasteride,

02:09:50.010 --> 02:09:53.190
and then you recheck it in
six months and it's 6.5,

02:09:53.190 --> 02:09:56.920
that is a huge concern, because
that's actually doubled.

02:09:56.920 --> 02:09:59.230
ANDREW HUBERMAN: I'm glad
you brought this up because I

02:09:59.230 --> 02:10:00.730
almost overlooked
the fact that I

02:10:00.730 --> 02:10:05.090
get a lot of questions about
drugs to offset hair loss.

02:10:05.090 --> 02:10:07.530
Most of those drugs are going
to operate through the DHT

02:10:07.530 --> 02:10:10.030
system-- the dihydrotestosterone
system-- for the reasons we

02:10:10.030 --> 02:10:10.863
talked about before.

02:10:10.863 --> 02:10:13.750
DHT receptors being on the
scalp and causing beard growth

02:10:13.750 --> 02:10:15.490
on the face.

02:10:15.490 --> 02:10:19.090
Is it the case that a number
of people taking things

02:10:19.090 --> 02:10:22.660
like Propecia and other
things to block the DHT

02:10:22.660 --> 02:10:25.480
or disrupt the DHT
pathway are going

02:10:25.480 --> 02:10:31.060
to experience diminished sex
drive, diminished motivation

02:10:31.060 --> 02:10:32.290
and general vigor?

02:10:32.290 --> 02:10:35.320
And if, so are there
alternatives like topical DHT

02:10:35.320 --> 02:10:37.750
antagonists that they
might use if they

02:10:37.750 --> 02:10:42.220
want to keep their hair, but
not have those negative effects?

02:10:42.220 --> 02:10:44.740
KYLE GILLETT: The way that
I think about hair loss

02:10:44.740 --> 02:10:48.850
is you have your fertilizers,
also known as growth agonist,

02:10:48.850 --> 02:10:51.130
and then you have
your anti-androgens.

02:10:51.130 --> 02:10:54.310
Whether they're systemic
or topical, there is both,

02:10:54.310 --> 02:10:57.550
but that's the general laymen's
way to think about hair loss.

02:10:57.550 --> 02:10:59.620
If you're only putting
fertilizer in your hair

02:10:59.620 --> 02:11:02.590
but you have androgenic alopecia
or male pattern baldness,

02:11:02.590 --> 02:11:04.415
then those hairs will
still miniaturize,

02:11:04.415 --> 02:11:06.040
and eventually, you'll
still have loss.

02:11:06.040 --> 02:11:08.830
ANDREW HUBERMAN: Such a
great word-- miniaturize.

02:11:08.830 --> 02:11:11.610
It's enough to send anybody
off to find a therapeutic.

02:11:11.610 --> 02:11:12.130
KYLE GILLETT: And
by the way, it's

02:11:12.130 --> 02:11:13.720
difficult to tell
if miniaturization

02:11:13.720 --> 02:11:16.492
is happening unless you
have a magnifying glass.

02:11:16.492 --> 02:11:17.200
And you can use--

02:11:17.200 --> 02:11:18.520
ANDREW HUBERMAN: I almost didn't
know-- for a second there,

02:11:18.520 --> 02:11:19.960
I didn't know whether or
not you were making a joke.

02:11:19.960 --> 02:11:21.220
You're talking about
miniaturization

02:11:21.220 --> 02:11:22.150
of the hair follicle.

02:11:22.150 --> 02:11:22.960
KYLE GILLETT: Correct.

02:11:22.960 --> 02:11:24.880
ANDREW HUBERMAN: So what can
reverse that miniaturization?

02:11:24.880 --> 02:11:26.020
Gosh, it's just a
fun word to say.

02:11:26.020 --> 02:11:27.395
I'm going to just
keep saying it.

02:11:27.395 --> 02:11:29.080
KYLE GILLETT: Each
individual has--

02:11:29.080 --> 02:11:31.210
again, we mentioned
the androgen receptor.

02:11:31.210 --> 02:11:33.745
Males only have one
androgen receptor gene

02:11:33.745 --> 02:11:35.390
that's on their X chromosome.

02:11:35.390 --> 02:11:38.050
So depending on how sensitive
that androgen receptor

02:11:38.050 --> 02:11:42.700
is and depending on the density
of the receptors in the hair

02:11:42.700 --> 02:11:46.930
follicle, you can have
an arbitrary threshold.

02:11:46.930 --> 02:11:48.910
And you don't know
what this threshold

02:11:48.910 --> 02:11:50.830
is until you start to
have miniaturization

02:11:50.830 --> 02:11:52.210
and loss of hair.

02:11:52.210 --> 02:11:55.570
But over the threshold,
the follicle will die

02:11:55.570 --> 02:11:57.400
and eventually the
stem cell will leave.

02:11:57.400 --> 02:12:00.670
But under the
threshold, you're OK.

02:12:00.670 --> 02:12:03.980
Every androgen binds to
the same androgen receptor.

02:12:03.980 --> 02:12:06.550
So there is nothing
special about DHT.

02:12:06.550 --> 02:12:11.350
DHT is just a stronger androgen.
So the higher your SHBG--

02:12:11.350 --> 02:12:15.700
things that increase SHBG
are beneficial for hair loss

02:12:15.700 --> 02:12:19.040
prevention because you have
less binding of that receptor.

02:12:19.040 --> 02:12:20.560
So if you think
about hair loss--

02:12:20.560 --> 02:12:22.750
specifically, androgenic
or male pattern

02:12:22.750 --> 02:12:26.200
baldness in the terms of
that androgen receptor

02:12:26.200 --> 02:12:28.510
and everything in
general binding to it--

02:12:28.510 --> 02:12:31.450
not just DHT, but also
testosterone-- it's helpful.

02:12:31.450 --> 02:12:34.000
It's just that DHT
is a huge battering

02:12:34.000 --> 02:12:36.040
ram whereas the other
androgens are just

02:12:36.040 --> 02:12:37.390
light presses on the door.

02:12:37.390 --> 02:12:38.390
ANDREW HUBERMAN: Got it.

02:12:38.390 --> 02:12:41.080
So are some of the
topical DHT receptor

02:12:41.080 --> 02:12:43.990
antagonists going to be a
better choice for people

02:12:43.990 --> 02:12:48.640
that want to maintain their
hair or grow more hair if they

02:12:48.640 --> 02:12:50.110
want to avoid side effects?

02:12:50.110 --> 02:12:51.640
KYLE GILLETT: Likely so.

02:12:51.640 --> 02:12:55.860
Some individuals
benefit from systemic--

02:12:55.860 --> 02:12:59.000
a systemic decrease in DHT
for a couple of reasons.

02:12:59.000 --> 02:13:01.240
One could be prostate and
then one could actually

02:13:01.240 --> 02:13:04.280
be hypertrophy of
the myocardium.

02:13:04.280 --> 02:13:08.090
So DHT also disproportionately
thickens the ventricle.

02:13:08.090 --> 02:13:09.730
So for someone on
TRT, that might

02:13:09.730 --> 02:13:11.830
be a benefit that is
prone to thickening

02:13:11.830 --> 02:13:14.150
of the ventricle at baseline.

02:13:14.150 --> 02:13:18.430
However, many people that have
just a bit of predisposition,

02:13:18.430 --> 02:13:22.780
they can use things that
are topical anti-androgens.

02:13:22.780 --> 02:13:24.910
Ketoconazole is one
of them, caffeine

02:13:24.910 --> 02:13:26.050
is actually another one.

02:13:26.050 --> 02:13:27.430
ANDREW HUBERMAN: Wait--
drinking caffeine?

02:13:27.430 --> 02:13:28.420
KYLE GILLETT: Topical caffeine.

02:13:28.420 --> 02:13:28.930
ANDREW HUBERMAN: Oh,
I was going to say

02:13:28.930 --> 02:13:30.430
my hair tends to
grow pretty fast,

02:13:30.430 --> 02:13:32.390
so it might be-- but I
drink a lot of caffeine.

02:13:32.390 --> 02:13:33.460
So topical caffeine?

02:13:33.460 --> 02:13:35.350
Really, rubbing
coffee on their head--

02:13:35.350 --> 02:13:35.590
KYLE GILLETT: Yes.

02:13:35.590 --> 02:13:37.690
ANDREW HUBERMAN: --or
taking caffeine tablets--

02:13:37.690 --> 02:13:40.570
and how does it-- wait, you
have to explain how this works?

02:13:40.570 --> 02:13:44.170
How do people get caffeine
into the hair follicle.

02:13:44.170 --> 02:13:47.260
KYLE GILLETT: Topically, the
caffeine enters the scalp

02:13:47.260 --> 02:13:48.910
and crowds out--

02:13:48.910 --> 02:13:52.540
somewhat crowds out the
androgen. It is a weak effect.

02:13:52.540 --> 02:13:56.110
It's likely just strong enough
to be clinically significant.

02:13:56.110 --> 02:13:59.200
Usually, caffeine is put into
formulations with other things

02:13:59.200 --> 02:14:03.490
like ketoconazole that are
also weak anti-androgens.

02:14:03.490 --> 02:14:06.650
Of note, spironolactone can
be prescribed topically,

02:14:06.650 --> 02:14:09.340
but it is absorbed
systemically because the size

02:14:09.340 --> 02:14:10.430
of the molecule.

02:14:10.430 --> 02:14:12.490
So unless your
doctor specifically

02:14:12.490 --> 02:14:14.740
prescribes that for you,
especially as a male,

02:14:14.740 --> 02:14:17.170
do not use topical
spironolactone.

02:14:17.170 --> 02:14:21.110
Topical finasteride is
also a smaller molecule,

02:14:21.110 --> 02:14:23.320
so it is also
systemically absorbed,

02:14:23.320 --> 02:14:26.770
but it is not extremely
well systemically absorbed.

02:14:26.770 --> 02:14:29.500
If you take topical
finasteride, then usually

02:14:29.500 --> 02:14:33.430
your systemic DHT will
decrease by about 30%.

02:14:33.430 --> 02:14:37.930
Topical dutasteride is likely a
tiny bit systemically absorbed,

02:14:37.930 --> 02:14:39.640
but it's unique
because it's half life

02:14:39.640 --> 02:14:41.930
is much faster at a lower dose.

02:14:41.930 --> 02:14:45.940
So topical dutasteride will
not affect your systemic DHT

02:14:45.940 --> 02:14:48.610
at all, and I've seen this
anecdotally on many people

02:14:48.610 --> 02:14:50.950
on topical dutasteride therapy.

02:14:50.950 --> 02:14:53.450
ANDREW HUBERMAN: We're going
