02:15:24.110 --> 02:15:25.890
KYLE GILLETT: Many
people report this.

02:15:25.890 --> 02:15:28.460
And the interesting
thing about turmeric

02:15:28.460 --> 02:15:31.460
is most of it's beneficial
action-- not all of it--

02:15:31.460 --> 02:15:34.037
some people benefit
from systemic turmeric.

02:15:34.037 --> 02:15:35.870
And some people that
can tolerate it-- well,

02:15:35.870 --> 02:15:38.060
it's actually great
for the prostate.

02:15:38.060 --> 02:15:41.750
But most of the action, it does
not need to be bioavailable.

02:15:41.750 --> 02:15:44.430
It acts on the gut microbiome.

02:15:44.430 --> 02:15:48.050
So you can take turmeric,
and if it is not absorbed--

02:15:48.050 --> 02:15:51.200
some turmeric is put in special
formulations like micellar,

02:15:51.200 --> 02:15:53.600
or liposomal, or complexed.

02:15:53.600 --> 02:15:55.820
But a lot of it is put
with black pepper fruit

02:15:55.820 --> 02:15:58.700
extract, which is also known
as bioperine, which is actually

02:15:58.700 --> 02:16:01.140
also a 5-alpha
reductase inhibitor

02:16:01.140 --> 02:16:03.440
and it affects liver cytochrome.

02:16:03.440 --> 02:16:06.260
And so many supplement companies
put this black pepper fruit

02:16:06.260 --> 02:16:06.920
extract--

02:16:06.920 --> 02:16:09.170
bioperine-- in
almost everything.

02:16:09.170 --> 02:16:11.510
So some people are
on really high doses,

02:16:11.510 --> 02:16:14.120
and that could
also be making most

02:16:14.120 --> 02:16:17.420
of the effect of people who
do not tolerate turmeric well.

02:16:17.420 --> 02:16:20.270
ANDREW HUBERMAN: Yeah, I avoid
turmeric like the plague based

02:16:20.270 --> 02:16:22.040
on that one previous
experience because it

02:16:22.040 --> 02:16:26.690
was clearly turmeric that
caused the negative effect.

02:16:26.690 --> 02:16:29.000
Coming off it, everything
reversed rapidly.

02:16:29.000 --> 02:16:31.712
And the bioperine-- the
black pepper extract--

02:16:31.712 --> 02:16:33.920
I also avoid that like the
plague based on everything

02:16:33.920 --> 02:16:35.030
you just said.

02:16:35.030 --> 02:16:38.690
I want my 5-alpha
reductase, I want my DHT

02:16:38.690 --> 02:16:42.139
to be optimized simply
because my understanding is

02:16:42.139 --> 02:16:45.591
DHT is the more
powerful androgen

02:16:45.591 --> 02:16:48.049
and it's the one that-- yes,
it causes a little bit of hair

02:16:48.049 --> 02:16:50.209
loss and I've got a few
patches here and there,

02:16:50.209 --> 02:16:51.855
but I'm willing
to live with that

02:16:51.855 --> 02:16:53.480
based on all the
other wonderful things

02:16:53.480 --> 02:16:56.360
that DHT optimization does.

02:16:56.360 --> 02:16:58.410
I'll quickly mention
a few other things.

02:16:58.410 --> 02:17:01.760
One, saw palmetto is
also a 5-alpha reductase

02:17:01.760 --> 02:17:04.549
inhibitor, but only a
couple of the isoenzymes.

02:17:04.549 --> 02:17:08.059
There's three main isoenzymes,
and a lot of the problem

02:17:08.059 --> 02:17:11.240
is that you're inhibiting
a couple of the isoenzymes,

02:17:11.240 --> 02:17:12.709
but not the other one.

02:17:12.709 --> 02:17:16.610
Finasteride inhibits 1 and 2.

02:17:16.610 --> 02:17:19.129
Dutasteride actually
inhibits all three.

02:17:19.129 --> 02:17:22.790
And finasteride
inhibits the isoenzyme

02:17:22.790 --> 02:17:26.360
that is in genital skin, but not
in the skin throughout the rest

02:17:26.360 --> 02:17:27.360
of your body.

02:17:27.360 --> 02:17:29.719
So a lot of the side
effects of finasteride,

02:17:29.719 --> 02:17:33.650
which is loss of sensation
and loss of erectile function,

02:17:33.650 --> 02:17:37.490
have to do with
the disconcordance

02:17:37.490 --> 02:17:40.677
between the sensitivity of
the genital skin and the skin.

02:17:40.677 --> 02:17:42.260
ANDREW HUBERMAN:
Again, another reason

02:17:42.260 --> 02:17:44.450
to not disrupt
5-alpha reductase.

02:17:44.450 --> 02:17:46.873
And we'll definitely get you
back on here to talk about--

02:17:46.873 --> 02:17:49.040
I think we should just do
a whole episode about DHT,

02:17:49.040 --> 02:17:50.748
because so often when
people are thinking

02:17:50.748 --> 02:17:54.033
about optimizing hormones,
especially males trying

02:17:54.033 --> 02:17:56.450
to optimize their hormones,
they're thinking testosterone,

02:17:56.450 --> 02:17:56.990
testosterone.

02:17:56.990 --> 02:17:58.400
Maybe nowadays, they
think a little bit more

02:17:58.400 --> 02:18:00.959
about free testosterone and
maybe they think about estrogen

02:18:00.959 --> 02:18:02.959
as also being important--
not to crush estrogen.

02:18:02.959 --> 02:18:06.830
But DHT is, at least to
my mind, the linchpin

02:18:06.830 --> 02:18:09.410
of so many of the things that
subjectively people are really

02:18:09.410 --> 02:18:12.876
focused on-- libido,
motivation, drive, et cetera.

02:18:12.876 --> 02:18:14.959
I have one final question--
it's just a brief one,

02:18:14.959 --> 02:18:18.139
but many of us have heard
that the BPAs that are present

02:18:18.139 --> 02:18:21.500
in plastic bottles and even
in certain aluminum cans

02:18:21.500 --> 02:18:24.320
and phthalates-- a
difficult word to pronounce,

02:18:24.320 --> 02:18:26.780
but a fun one
nonetheless-- phthalates--

02:18:26.780 --> 02:18:31.010
and work by Dr. Shanna Swan has
shown that phthalate exposure

02:18:31.010 --> 02:18:32.120
to the fetus--

02:18:32.120 --> 02:18:34.730
to pregnant mothers and
to fetuses very likely

02:18:34.730 --> 02:18:37.639
is negatively impacting sperm
counts, testosterone levels,

02:18:37.639 --> 02:18:42.350
and even changing genitalia
size for the worse in males

02:18:42.350 --> 02:18:44.299
nowadays.

02:18:44.299 --> 02:18:47.480
I saw a beautiful lecture that
Dr. Shanna Swan did on this

02:18:47.480 --> 02:18:49.462
when I was in Copenhagen.
And it's very clear

02:18:49.462 --> 02:18:51.379
that it's negatively
impacting the male fetus.

02:18:51.379 --> 02:18:53.030
She was also on Joe
Rogan's podcast.

02:18:53.030 --> 02:18:54.830
I hope to get her
on this podcast.

02:18:54.830 --> 02:18:57.139
However, what she
